=\"message\">Errrrrr I\u2019ve yet to get my physical dragon blooded book that a paid for via kickstarter?<br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> Hard to shell out on another before that last project has actually given me what I paid for last time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, you have to make your own decisions about how to spend your money. However, the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter stated when they expected to deliver the product. From the FAQ for the DB Kickstarter: &quot;The estimated delivery date listed on your Reward Tier indicates expected fulfillment for Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought. For the PDF, it is expected to be delivered to all backers by February 2019. For the deluxe hardcover edition, it is expected to be delivered to all backers who have correctly confirmed their shipping address by December 2019. If the projects are completed before these dates, they will be sent to backers as soon as they are ready.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, they've delivered the PDF ahead of time, and I would expect the same for the hard copy, but they're certainly not failing to deliver what they've promised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T14:07:24-08:00","id":1283999,"title":"","content":"Le sigh. Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Want the book but it\u2019s hard to justify the $100\u2019s I spend on the things when I\u2019ve yet to get the last thing I paid for.<br /> <br /> But your right, it\u2019s says the delivery dates right there. <br /> <br /> Just leaves a bad taste I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T16:58:54-08:00","id":1284036,"title":"","content":"Something that might help is to understand that, back in the days before kickstarter and pdf books, we generally only found out about books when they hit the shelves. Maybe they started hyping stuff in magazines and things before hand, but they mostly timed those ads to coincide with the physical release. <br /> <br /> However, the books still took a couple years to make. They just didn\u2019t have any reason to tell us about it before they could sell us a copy. But the writers and developers for those books were all two books down the line before we ever saw the physical product.<br /> <br /> By backing the Kickstarter, you get to join the Writers and Developers on Development Time. You get secret access to the book over a year in advance, before the general public. And you potentially get a spiffy faux Leather bound copy of the book when it arrives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T06:13:37-08:00","id":1284115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steel_in_sea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1283999#post1283999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Le sigh. Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Want the book but it\u2019s hard to justify the $100\u2019s I spend on the things when I\u2019ve yet to get the last thing I paid for.<br /> <br /> But your right, it\u2019s says the delivery dates right there. <br /> <br /> Just leaves a bad taste I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel the same. I'm not accusing anyone of acting in bad faith, but at the same time I did skip a bunch of OP kickstarters I might have gotten in on had I not still been waiting on the 3e Exalted core. I had thought that being basically content-complete before they started the KS would have sped up the process (for DBs) more than it did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T08:55:15-08:00","id":1284145,"title":"","content":"I am both excited for and wary of the Lunar kickstarter, much as I was for the DB kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: I am a very getable consumer, and I'll buy the products all day long once you get me. Exalted 2E got me. D&amp;D 5E got me. Exalted 3E has yet to get me. (I backed the 3E kickstarter, I dropped the DB kickstarter after seeing the manuscript and am undecided on buying WFHW or The Realm, and we'll see how I feel about Lunars.) I really hope that Lunars gets me.<br /> <br /> As I reflect on what I just said, it's funny that, in some ways, I'm much more discerning about the gaming products that I buy now, when I have money, than I was when I was in high school and college, when I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T09:53:40-08:00","id":1284153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284145#post1284145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am both excited for and wary of the Lunar kickstarter, much as I was for the DB kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: I am a very getable consumer, and I'll buy the products all day long once you get me. Exalted 2E got me. D&amp;D 5E got me. Exalted 3E has yet to get me. (I backed the 3E kickstarter, I dropped the DB kickstarter after seeing the manuscript and am undecided on buying WFHW or The Realm, and we'll see how I feel about Lunars.) I really hope that Lunars gets me..</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m curious, what made you drop the Kickstarter after seeing the manuscript?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:07:46-08:00","id":1284155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284153#post1284153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m curious, what made you drop the Kickstarter after seeing the manuscript?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it the charmset? It was the charmset wasn't it? Much rage over the charmset did I witness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:20:14-08:00","id":1284156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284155#post1284155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was it the charmset? It was the charmset wasn't it? Much rage over the charmset did I witness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the two main complaints I saw there was that it was underpowered and a couple charms just didn\u2019t seem to work properly, the later mostly got fixed in the update that we just got. The former I understand, especially going from the huge drop of Solar down to DB, but I don\u2019t necessarily agree with since a chargen DB brawler can still easily dismantle a pair of blood apes with her bare hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:24:29-08:00","id":1284158,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-Blooded should now be more powerful than they ever were before, so I don\u2019t see why their Charms should seem weak to anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:59:29-08:00","id":1284167,"title":"","content":"Dragonblood are much stronger compared to Solars than they were in 2nd edition, but that's mostly because Solars are weaker (or, as I'd prefer to put it, no longer break the combat system) rather than DBs are stronger.<br /> I haven't played a 3rd ed DB myself, so this is theorycraft, but compared to 2nd ed DBs (which I played a lot) they seem stronger socially but not stronger in other ways. They're more evened out; there are more good builds now, that you wouldn't have played in 2nd ed, like Resistance; but I don't think a Fire Aspect dodge/swordsman with 13 combat charms and high breeding is stronger now than in 2nd ed. I'd say they're weaker. And having more charms makes you stronger, but that doesn't impact how people rate charms individually.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I don't think DBs are too weak (though maybe too fiddly), but I can understand why some people do think that.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I don't think that will be an issue with Lunars. The previewed charms don't seem weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T11:31:17-08:00","id":1284175,"title":"","content":"edit: deletion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T12:29:06-08:00","id":1284187,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Lunar charms are badass. From what I\u2019ve seen of them they\u2019re not as powerful as the Solar ones directly, so that might irk some people, but they seem to be more versatile, which is a power in its own right.<br /> <br /> I think that looking at specific charms, especially combat ones, DBs look and feel weaker. Like for example Ringing Anvil Onslaught became Harnessed Firestorm Assault, which tends to have less attacks, has a reset, requires fire aura and can\u2019t be taken off chargen. It also isn\u2019t great unless you\u2019re maxed. On the other hand it also boosts your damage nicely now. <br /> <br /> Also a lot of charms are just not very punchy conpared to what the baseline is, like Crossfire Flash, which is almost strictly worse than the excellency, except 10s count as 3 for its bonus dice. Of course where it\u2019s meant to be used is in conjunction with a full excellency to nab yourself what are effectively better non-charm dice. They work out to eventually be better than an excellency anyway. <br /> <br /> The non-combat charms are pretty comparable though, and actually in 3e I\u2019d say in a lot of ways the new ones are much more impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T13:23:03-08:00","id":1284196,"title":"","content":"Also their charms actually work on solars now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T13:53:18-08:00","id":1284206,"title":"","content":"Woohoohoo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T15:50:45-08:00","id":1284228,"title":"","content":"Charms are probably going to be split between two previews again right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T21:36:55-08:00","id":1284276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284228#post1284228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms are probably going to be split between two previews again right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the volume of charms in these splats, I figure they have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T23:31:49-08:00","id":1284291,"title":"","content":"Is there any actual information on how Lunars work, now? Or will we only find out when the Kickstarter hits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T23:57:11-08:00","id":1284295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284291#post1284291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any actual information on how Lunars work, now? Or will we only find out when the Kickstarter hits?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a big question, and I'm not sure what it is you want to know specifically.<br /> <br /> We've had a few Lunar previews already: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">a selection of Lunar Charms</a>, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/solar-bonds-exalted-3rd-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">3e's Solar Bond</a> and some of the Charms that benefit from it, and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-lunar-exalted-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">an overview of Lunar history</a> and the modern Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> We know Lunars get two new Charm keywords: Protean, for Charms that gain benefits with particular animal forms, and Totemic, for Charms that gain benefits with particular spirit shapes. Knacks are done and gone, with shapeshifting being integrated into the Charmset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T00:24:08-08:00","id":1284298,"title":"","content":"There's also a Lunar NPC who has been released, Eska of the Seven Blades, though there may be changes between her and the final text.<br /> <br /> There's also, somewhere on here, a thread started by some playtesters who talked about some of the charms.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, what else. Lunars get 2 caste attributes and 2 favoured attributes, except Casteless who get 3 favoured. They also get a discount on other charms (so I'm guessing 9xp? Lunars use the same 8/10 cost as Solars now), have anima powers, and don't turn into Chinaera.<br /> Being a Chimaera is a charm tree now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T09:20:38-08:00","id":1284359,"title":"","content":"Two caste and two favoured? That's really interesting, aside from anima abilities that's effectively just pick four.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T09:35:46-08:00","id":1284362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284295#post1284295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a big question, and I'm not sure what it is you want to know specifically.<br /> <br /> We've had a few Lunar previews already: <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/&amp;quot;]a</a> selection of Lunar Charms[/URL], <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/solar-bonds-exalted-3rd-edition/&amp;quot;]3e's</a> Solar Bond[/URL] and some of the Charms that benefit from it, and <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-lunar-exalted-exalted/&amp;quot;]an</a> overview of Lunar history[/URL] and the modern Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> We know Lunars get two new Charm keywords: Protean, for Charms that gain benefits with particular animal forms, and Totemic, for Charms that gain benefits with particular spirit shapes. Knacks are done and gone, with shapeshifting being integrated into the Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that\u2019s a useful answer. Vance talked a little about how the tone was shifting away from barbarian pulp fantasy and more into god/monster dichotomy a couple years ago, and I wanted to know how they were implementing that.<br /> <br /> The material you've linked looks all right. I don\u2019t recall reading the word \u2018barbarian\u2019 even once in any of it, which already seems like a huge step in the right direction in tone. Another of the failures of Lunars up to now is that they've focused a lot on animal shapeshifting, which isn't very interesting. It feels mundane, and is simply not a very useful tool compared to the rest of the supernatural abilities on display. The fact that they're explicitly going for the walking gods + monster in myth angle is good: those thematics are broad enough that they should have a lot of things to play with for the Charmset, and an interesting direction to take shapeshifting in. Obviously, building shapeshifting into the Charmset (in any way) is a good thing. My preferred angle would have been &quot;protean shapeshifter&quot; and simply make all Lunar magic themed around optimizing your form (and potentially your mind) for the task at hand, but this can work.<br /> <br /> It's a shame that they went with the same warrior/trickster shaman divide of old: the role of the shaman in particular is unclear and has never been well supported as an archetype. I really don't see how having an archetype that's mainly mental-based while having large chunks of the mental abilities' domains restricted (&quot;Lunars are the most self-sufficient Exalt type because when everyone's limited to fighting with clubs they come out on top, and they're not good at building things or countries in the first place&quot;) is going to be a good idea. It hasn't tied into shapeshifting at all either\u2014as opposed to warrior and trickster. Rethinking this would have been better. If they're going in this direction again, I hope they at least have useful things for mental Lunars to do. Fortunately, ditching the whole barbarian thing opens some doors here.<br /> <br /> The attribute-based Charmset seems more like a sacred cow than a mechanical innovation that had any point in previous editions. Most of the subsystems in the game were tied to specific abilities, which meant that the premise of having broad attribute-based magic that applied across multiple abilities was false for basically everything but the weapon-based combat abilities and some presence/performance social stuff. At best, it was a combo package in which you had prerequisites in many different somewhat-related areas, and it wasn't a very appealing deal. 2/2 is a massive improvement over 3/1, at least, considering how redundant some attribute pairs ended up being. I'm not happy to see it come back, but maybe they'll do something interesting with it this time around.<br /> <br /> The war v. the Realm and the Bronze faction reads well. These Lunars don't give off the vibe of being losers and victims with impractical strategies, which is a nice change of pace.<br /> <br /> Somehow, I'm cautiously optimistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","user":"Black Paper Moon","date":". 02-02-2019, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T12:26:03-08:00","id":1284380,"title":"","content":"I've played with 2 caste and 2 favourite for years: the guy who wrote the Lunar charmset for 2nd ed recommended it (someone else wrote the character gen, and he felt it made them underpowered). <br /> <br /> It works really well: it's still distinctly that Caste (as opposed to, say, having a Dex/Cha/Per/Wits Full Moon, which would be silly), but it's more flexible.<br /> <br /> It's also important if a Casteless Lunar becomes a certain Caste, because you don't lose any Favoured attributes, which would be weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T18:29:47-08:00","id":1284428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284196#post1284196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also their charms actually work on solars now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't really argue that a Fire Aspect swordsman is weaker than in previous Editions, now that he can actually use Portentous Comet Deflection against ANYTHING, and the opponent must used a specialized &quot;no, you can't clash this&quot; Charm to bypass it.<br /> <br /> There's also the power to use Dragon-Graced Weapon to create ANYTHING, from swords to shields to spears to whips. That's some flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T22:00:53-08:00","id":1284445,"title":"","content":"Why would a Fire Aspect use Melee charms to defend? No one used Portentious Comet, you used your DDV of 10 (doable as a starting character), and pumped it to 14 for 4m. 16 with a 2-pt stunt. And being able to make all kinds of weapons just isn't as scary as doubling the raw damage of your Strength+Dire Lance for 2m (Speed 3, of course).<br /> And let's not forget your excellency cost 4m for 8 dice. And the free reflexives were a big deal in 2.0.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, compare the old DB perfect dodge to its 3.0 version. It used to be an actual perfect defence. 5m, 1wp, completely dodge any attack. There are no DB charms that good, defensively, now.<br /> And I think that's fine, because the combat system is different. All the Solar perfect defences have been seriously nerfed.<br /> But I can understand why someone might go &quot;Where's my perfect dodge gone? Why is Revelation of Associates Hunch no longer so powerful that Solars look upon it with envy? These charms are weak!&quot; and miss the big picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-03-2019, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T22:10:41-08:00","id":1284448,"title":"","content":"Now, getting back to Lunars...<br /> <br /> Lunars' 2nd ed charms included a lot of charms that were just Solar charms, but worse. So I think the 3rd ed charmset might be so different to the 2nd ed one that people won't compare them.<br /> Or they'll compare them to Solars' 3rd ed charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T22:36:55-08:00","id":1284449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284448#post1284448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, getting back to Lunars...<br /> <br /> Lunars' 2nd ed charms included a lot of charms that were just Solar charms, but worse. So I think the 3rd ed charmset might be so different to the 2nd ed one that people won't compare them.<br /> Or they'll compare them to Solars' 3rd ed charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that the Lunar Charmset has fundamental effects that other Exalted (thus far) can't duplicate. Its not just &quot;I can become everything!&quot; shapeshifting, but stuff like the &quot;I don't need Dex for anything combat related&quot; style charms as well. (I can imagine, and have already seen, people getting mad Salty that Lunars get this schtick while precious golden demigods still have to max Dex if they want to Invincible Sword Princess)<br /> <br /> It makes for very versatile, cheap and most of all effective (as Solars in the broad strokes) characters for Lunar players, and that is always going to put a smile on my face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-03-2019, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T00:16:20-08:00","id":1284455,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> A good example is a charm my character, Dr Soma, has, called Blood-And-Tear Elixir Cultivation.<br /> <br /> It's 5m, Simple.<br /> This lets you make medicine out of your body that counts as exceptional equipment to treat a specific malady. If you use it in the same scene to treat the malady, you can re-roll some 1s (and keep re-rolling them if you've suffered it yourself).<br /> <br /> Exceptional equipment is, what, +2 dice? Re-rolling some 1s, not that great. And as making the medicine is Simple, it's not very useful in combat.<br /> Compared to the Solar charms that add dice or successes to Medicine rolls, it seems pretty weak...<br /> <br /> This charm is excellent! You can make medicine for a specific malady, just straight out of your body! That's so incredibly flexible.<br /> Last session I discovered a guy dying of a rare poison. I diagnosed it, but rather than having to go and search for the antidote while he died, I just cut my hand and squeezed out the cure for that specific poison right then and there.<br /> <br /> It's not raw power. If you want 20 successes, Solars are a way to go. But with Solars I frequently find myself in a position where the charms I have just aren't useful. With a Lunar, your powers are often more flexible and... how do I explain this... give you new stuff you can do, rather than making you better at stuff a mortal can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously not all Lunar charms are like that. Eska has stuff like:<br /> Gleaming Crescent Block (4m, Some 1s take away attacker's successes. If your Parry succeeds, you can activate Coiled Serpent Strikes for no initiative cost)<br /> Instinct-Driven Beast Method (3, +1 success to a movement roll. If you succeed at an opposed roll, gain 1 initiative, and the opponent loses 1 initiative if you're in an animal form with a Speed Bonus)<br /> Dream-Weaving Voice (3m. Double 9s on an Inspire roll)<br /> <br /> That's not really mind-blowing stuff. But these are decent work-horse charms that a starting character will want. I haven't got in a fight yet, but I expect to use Gleaming Crescent Block a lot with my Snake-style Parry, mostly to activate Coiled Serpent Strikes for a 2m counter-attack. And I think most social characters would pick up Dream-Weaving Voice.<br /> <br /> And if you look at the Essence 1 charms with no prerequisites that have been previewed, we've got:<br /> Steel Paw Style<br /> Heart-Drinking Allure<br /> Memory-Drinking Meditation<br /> Blood-Geas Binding<br /> Moon-Follows-Sun Assurance<br /> <br /> These are all pretty good, fun charms.<br /> <br /> I actually think of the charms shown so far, the one I rate least for most characters is Octopus-and-Spider Barrage, but if you combo it with some other stuff and you're a Yeddim/Giant Spider/The Kraken, it's decent.<br /> (And I think others will rate it more.)<br /> <br /> Now, obviously, they probably wouldn't have chosen really dull, weak charms to be previewed. But Lunars aren't supposed to be the bottom line of charm power like Dragonblood, and the nature of their magic (shapechanging, shamanism and raw animal power) compared to Dragonblood (elementalism, being really good at human stuff, and combining the two) I think lends itself less to &quot;this charm just lets you re-roll stuff on a roll&quot; and more to &quot;this charm lets you do something weird&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-03-2019, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T00:32:52-08:00","id":1284460,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I wonder if Lunars will still be able to cross-apply Attribute charms? Ie use a Charisma charm that gives +1 success on Persuasion rolls and apply it to a Manipulation roll.<br /> <br /> If they're making attacks with Strength and parrying with Stamina (using Steel Paw Style, etc), they kind of need to be able to apply charms that are probably in Dexterity (not excellencies, you could just use your Strength or Stamina excellency on the attack roll, after all).<br /> And Strength likely has charms that apply to attack rolls even when you're rolling Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T01:30:26-08:00","id":1284465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284445#post1284445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I can understand why someone might go &quot;Where's my perfect dodge gone? Why is Revelation of Associates Hunch no longer so powerful that Solars look upon it with envy? These charms are weak!&quot; and miss the big picture.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's like there were people who looked at MoEP: Lunars and complained about it nerfing Deadly Beastman Transformation. Not many, but it really was a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T02:12:00-08:00","id":1284471,"title":"","content":"Ha! Oh, that's great.<br /> <br /> And probably a decent comparison.<br /> Like Lunars no longer having Dex 8, there's a good reason Revelation of Associates Hunch (a charm so powerful that 2.5 tried to nerf it... and instead made it even more powerful!) no longer is as good as it was. And Five-Dragon Force Blow (the single charm responsible for the most PC deaths in games I played) simply no longer exists. And that Dragonblood can no longer get Hearthstone Bracers, a Reinforced Breastplate, and an artefact weapon without spending any bonus points, or have a mote pool as good as a Solar (or at Essence 2, possibly better).<br /> <br /> Though, to be fair, I think the DB players have slightly more leg to stand on than people complaining about DBT. Charms like &quot;4m; ignore 2 point of soak, 4 if you aimed&quot;, don't really seem that hot. Or interesting. You have to look at them as a bonus on top of the excellency, or as something with growth potential that'll become more powerful when your essence goes up. Or, you know, you should instead look at their better charms (but the best charms of course, are not the ones you first read when you start reading a tree). But I can see how a quick skim might make people think DBs are really weak.<br /> I think also there seems to be a lot of people whose games never get to Essence 3, so all the cool Signature charms are, to them, something they'll never play with, they only get the starting charms, which of course are weaker.<br /> (Whereas, to me, never playing any game with Essence lower than 4, the only difference is between Essence 5 charms and not-Essence 5 charms.)<br /> <br /> There's also some DB charms that got boosted in the Errata phase, so now they're decent, but they were weak when the manuscript first came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T08:48:39-08:00","id":1284507,"title":"","content":"I've got a Lunar coming up in our Chronicle who specifically treats ideas, faiths, and arguments as her prey. That's absent having an official book, but it seems pretty Lunar to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T09:47:41-08:00","id":1284523,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, that's an interesting concept. What's her caste?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T10:16:55-08:00","id":1284536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284523#post1284523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, that's an interesting concept. What's her caste?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think my players come by here too often, but just in case... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> She'll probably be introduced in our next story arc, so all the details aren't together yet. I have her down as a No Moon, in that she operates in a very conceptual and esoteric fashion. She could equally be a Changing Moon in that she does a lot of social influence.<br /> <br /> Her name is Judy Booplesnoot (a moniker which she hates, and given to her by other Lunars making good-natured fun of her. Her actual name is Judith Bindlesnert, and she comes from a family of scavenger lords in the Threshold. Unlike most, the Bindlesnerts went to some considerable effort to recover lost lore and piece it together, rather than grab-n-sell. They've got some libraries and accessible collections, and do business as copyists and advisors as well. This part is all to capture some of my players' characters' flags, since they have an interest in recovering lore.<br /> <br /> She writes subversive literature under a variety of pen names. Her works have already been showing up, though we haven't established their significance or relationships yet. She uses them to &quot;hunt&quot; ideas that she wishes to critique or destroy. <br /> <br /> I'm planning to play her as a subtle and savage author and critic, who's actually approachable - even adorable - in person. She's the bunny with a shotgun, in fact, that I requested in the character art thread. I'm planning for her to be introduced by one of our characters' Lunar Mates, and that Judy will be very attractive to a particular character who's our lore-master.<br /> <br /> <br /> The works I've got her down as having written fall into a few categories...<br /> <br /> The Romances of the Sevens are collection of melodramatic romances - in the sense of the Romance of the Three Kingdoms - by an &quot;unknown&quot; author. They have enough similarities to each other and all have &quot;seven&quot; in the title, in order to generate interest in collecting them and speculation about them.<ul><li>Seven Seasons</li> <li>Seven Romances of Jade and Steel</li> <li>Seven Serenities of the Lost Shogunate</li> <li>Six Journeys (this one appears to be an &quot;unfinished&quot; work, also to fuel collectability and speculation)</li> <li>Seven Nights Across Calibration</li> <li>Seven Ships Fireworks</li> </ul><br /> <br /> A variety of Nunsploitation (with credit to folks on the forums here) written as trashy romance - in the modern sense of Harlequin novels - or ero-manga. They're packed with subtle critique and contradictions of the Immaculate Faith, and its adherents, and the social hierarchy of the Realm and elsewhere. They're by a variety of alleged authors, and inspire a lot of imitations and counterfeits of various quality.<ul><li>The Lonely Mask</li> <li>The Tourist's Guide to Penguins</li> <li>The Priestess whose Robes Turned Blue</li> <li>The Boat Hidden in the Lilies</li> <li>The Thing that Mayflies Know</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And finally, straight-up critiques, written to directly confront whatever idea she's hunting. Most of these are aimed at the Immaculate Faith and the Realm in general.<ul><li>Faith inside Fire</li> <li>Bitter and Sweet</li> <li>Five Discussions</li> <li>Illustrious and Mediocre</li> <li>Siblings Separated</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If she becomes a popular NPC, she might also novelize the PC's stories, packaging their legend and defending it from detractors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A bit much for an answer, but I had her notes right open, and thought it might be fun to bounce ideas around about how a mental/conceptual Lunar might work and hunt. <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T22:37:06-08:00","id":1284665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284471#post1284471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, to be fair, I think the DB players have slightly more leg to stand on than people complaining about DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it usually comes from basically the same place. My Caste/Aspect worked, sure others didn't... but fuck the people who want to play them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-04-2019, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T08:11:30-08:00","id":1284712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284291#post1284291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any actual information on how Lunars work, now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Our most recent information is that shapeshifting into any other shape is a miscellaneous action which cannot be flurried with an attack, you can stay in hybrid shape indefinitely but in Deadly Beastman Transformation for one scene, and shifting into your hybrid shape is a Simple Charm which can make DBT reflexive, and shifting into DBT separately from HBT is also a Simple Charm. Using DBT reduces your resonance-affinity with artifacts by one level, cutting you off from Resonant effects and Evocations. You can use Martial Arts style and Charms in DBT, but not in any animal form (though I would make an exception for Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style, which doesn't care about your body so much as your voice). Being in an animal form does not interfere with Evocations except that most animal forms are incapable of using weapons designed for humanoid hands. Returning to your base human form is always free and reflexive.<br /> <br /> All of this should create a level of exclusivity that encourages specialization and differentiation.<br /> <br /> If you want to freely use Martial Arts and Evocations, you can avoid DBT and limit yourself to Hybrid Body Transformation to play a Katana Catgirl or a Firewand Foxgirl. If your totem doesn't offer any mutations you particularly care for, you can skip Hybrid Body Transformation and still fight like Bayonetta with her crazy Strength and Dexterity Charms, Martial Arts, and many Evocations.<br /> <br /> Trying to assume DBT and a Martial Arts Form Charm in the same fight could require two whole rounds of set up if you can't manage the reflexive activation condition of the Form.<br /> <br /> Trying to fight exclusively as a lion, tiger, bear, or wolf helps with buying up all of the latent abilities of your chosen battle-form. You probably also don't want to invest in Martial Arts, and you're much more limited in terms of the artifacts and Evocations you can employ.<br /> <br /> Trying to fight exclusively as a T-Rex or similarly gigantic beast is possible from character generation, but the cost is staggering and the exhaustion risky. Plus, not all battlefields are appropriate for shapes that size.<br /> <br /> If you're fighting like Teen Titan's Beast Boy, by constantly shifting between animal forms (using the Charm that makes it easier/faster to assume other forms), attempting to switch to DBT will really slow you down because it is a Simple-type Charm. DBT is something special, but not in a way that makes turning into a tiger, bear, or gorilla worthless.<br /> <br /> Even if you're not playing a master animal-shapeshifter, any Lunar build can plan on flurrying a disengage with the action to turn into a bird (or turning into a bird after successfully disengaging) to run away from a fight that turns ugly. If you're not planning to stick around, then it doesn't matter what Simple-type set-up Charms you're effectively tossing aside.<br /> <br /> We don't know if assuming an animal form cancels any Martial Arts Form you're currently using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:13:11-08:00","id":1284786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1283477#post1283477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, I need to find room in my february budget<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope I won't have ti give up a new sporran to go with my kilts....</div> </div> </div> </div>I am getting my second root canal. But I think I can get one book for me and another for another forumite that has fiscal issues getting it. Someone helped me get my Dragonblooded Book, CoughGlamourweavercough, so I will pay it forward. Also I promised to get someone Scroll of the Monk II but that got cancelled and turned into 3rd ed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:16:20-08:00","id":1284787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1283477#post1283477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, I need to find room in my february budget<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope I won't have ti give up a new sporran to go with my kilts....</div> </div> </div> </div>You really need the sporran. Holding things is an issue otherwise. It feels like you\u2019re in an RPG with zero inventory space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T14:00:27-08:00","id":1284799,"title":"","content":"But, what if the Kickstarter has a reward tier for a sporran to carry your book in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T14:18:59-08:00","id":1284802,"title":"","content":"That reminds me... I wonder how set Lunars are for being able to carry stuff Elsewhere. Seems pretty handy for shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T14:48:05-08:00","id":1284807,"title":"","content":"They used to have a Wits tree about it.<br /> Now, there's a previewed Wits charm that lets you pull an item out of your pocket that you declare you made/stole/bought/found earlier.<br /> I wondered if either a) that was part of a tree that includes Elsewhere charms, or b)Lunars don't have much straight-up Elsewhere stuff, but have a number of charms that essentially do something similar but with different fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T21:43:11-08:00","id":1284887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284802#post1284802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me... I wonder how set Lunars are for being able to carry stuff Elsewhere. Seems pretty handy for shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar clothes and gear going Elsewhere when they shift to animal forms has been pretty standard since 1e. I doubt that will change now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T23:34:39-08:00","id":1284896,"title":"","content":"Seven Days!<br /> <br /> ........<br /> <br /> .....f4, f4, f4, f4, f4, f4......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T00:30:35-08:00","id":1284900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284807#post1284807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They used to have a Wits tree about it.<br /> Now, there's a previewed Wits charm that lets you pull an item out of your pocket that you declare you made/stole/bought/found earlier.<br /> I wondered if either a) that was part of a tree that includes Elsewhere charms, or b)Lunars don't have much straight-up Elsewhere stuff, but have a number of charms that essentially do something similar but with different fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's Elsewhere and elsewhere. Lunars having access to what was basically a Sanctum was one of those things that muddied their thematics. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T00:37:04-08:00","id":1284902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284900#post1284900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's Elsewhere and elsewhere. Lunars having access to what was basically a Sanctum was one of those things that muddied their thematics.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Squirreling things away to hide muddied the thematics of the literal &quot;I can become a Squirrel-Girl expy&quot; Exalted?<br /> <br /> You lost me somewhere.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T02:57:35-08:00","id":1284908,"title":"","content":"I think Lioness is talking about the Elsewhere den charms.<br /> Which are supposed to be about, well, having a den, but came off more as having a pocket dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T07:24:30-08:00","id":1284959,"title":"","content":"Too many Charms were devoted to doing stuff and making things in the Elsewhere Den which would never matter in Creation itself. There's no reason for having a Wyld-Shaping Technique in your Elsewhere Den because you couldn't take anything out of the Den.<br /> <br /> At most, you would want a more streamlined Charm that would let you create any sort of workshop for crafting with the raw materials you brought in, or any sort of medical facility for healing yourself or someone else you dragged in. So, something more like Craftsman Needs No Tools and Contagion-Curing Touch than Wyld-Shaping Technique.<br /> <br /> Giving a Lunar the ability to create a whole other, self-contained world apart from Creation that could never interact with Creation and which ceased to exist when the Lunar left it and within which the Lunar could not be affected or dragged out... it just sort of encouraged Lunar Exalted to leave Creation and never come back. And the Lunar Exalted already suffered from being relegated to the fringes of the setting and forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T09:21:46-08:00","id":1284978,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I never actually saw anyone take those charms, so I'm not sure how they'd end up working in practice.<br /> <br /> Did any of you see them used?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T09:43:36-08:00","id":1284987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284978#post1284978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I never actually saw anyone take those charms, so I'm not sure how they'd end up working in practice.<br /> <br /> Did any of you see them used?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never. But I really liked the idea of Lunars being able to make some Wyld tricks. What I saw used were the mutiple action charms where one hit seemed to sprout from several different directions. That was a neat use of dimensional magic IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T11:21:51-08:00","id":1285013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284978#post1284978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I never actually saw anyone take those charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. The Charms wouldn't have enabled stories that people get together in a group to tell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284987#post1284987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never. But I really liked the idea of Lunars being able to make some Wyld tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Robert Vance has said that Lunars will have better Wyld Charms than Ritual of Lunar Stability while obviously not reaching the craziness of Wyld-Shaping Technique.<br /> <br /> Because the Lunar Exalted aren't the victims of the Wyld, anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I saw used were the mutiple action charms where one hit seemed to sprout from several different directions. That was a neat use of dimensional magic IMO. </div> </div> </div>That's the sort of stuff I think Getimians will get to do, anywhere. Also the time-dilation stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T11:27:20-08:00","id":1285016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1285013#post1285013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course not. The Charms wouldn't have enabled stories that people get together in a group to tell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could take your circle with you to your pocket dimension. That's pretty useful.<br /> But you had to invest quite a lot to be able to do that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T15:05:56-08:00","id":1285063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284802#post1284802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me... I wonder how set Lunars are for being able to carry stuff Elsewhere. Seems pretty handy for shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is purely a feature of our Aeon Exalted setting hack, and entirely in absence of any manuscript. <br /> <br /> But! <br /> <br /> Our Lunars will have a Lair, inspired by but not directly lifted from Beast. The Lair can connect to any place where the Lunar has a territory, including places in other Aeons. (Aeons being a pocket realm, such as the dead corpus of a long ago nation or religion.) The Lair is attached directly as a feature of the Exaltation, and there are some story elements for Lunars going on experimenting with and building through them. Inside the Lair, all the Lunar's shapes are present, as is their panoply. So, they have a hideout, a thematically intrinsic way to travel around, and built-in storage equivalent to Elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Whether this will require some Charms or be completely intrinsic from the start is yet to be determined - in our Chronicle we're still doing the initial set of reveals about the existence of Aeons (*) and dropping a few clues about how they work. By the time we have the Lunars manuscripts in our eager paws, my players will know pretty well what they're dealing with. In the meantime, the NPC Lunars have an unexplained talent for vanishing entirely out of Creation and popping up somewhere else in a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> Presented purely to share the idea!<br /> <br /> <br /> (*) Coming Saturday's session will have us going to our first semi-stable Aeon. I'm looking forward to sending the Solars into the dead husk of the Empire of Xaarr. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T16:52:57-08:00","id":1285078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284362#post1284362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while having large chunks of the mental abilities' domains restricted (&amp;quot;Lunars are the most self-sufficient Exalt type because when everyone's limited to fighting with clubs they come out on top, and they're not good at building things or countries in the first place&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is incredibly no longer going to be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T23:32:31-08:00","id":1285136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284902#post1284902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Squirreling things away to hide muddied the thematics of the literal &quot;I can become a Squirrel-Girl expy&quot; Exalted?<br /> <br /> You lost me somewhere.<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Squirrel Girl doesn't store things in pocket dimensions.<br /> <br /> Even if she did, the argument that Lunars should because of that would be about as compelling as &quot;Lunars should get nine lives because of Catwoman in Batman Returns&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T23:51:48-08:00","id":1285140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1285136#post1285136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Squirrel Girl doesn't store things in pocket dimensions.<br /> <br /> Even if she did, the argument that Lunars should because of that would be about as compelling as &quot;Lunars should get nine lives because of Catwoman in Batman Returns&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take, which doesn't necessarily have to be your take, is as follows:<br /> <br /> There is nothing in Solar thematics that make Elsewhere a thing for them too.<br /> <br /> <b>I am god-king, ruling benevolently by the Power of the Sun, Secure in my Ability to be the Very Best at what I apply my Skill to</b>... Also Hammerspace.<br /> <br /> See, nothing about it makes sense. But, because Elsewhere is a thing in Creation, they get to interact with it in a way that kind of links back to their thematics (i.e. they can build a sanctum in it, because great at building e.t.c.)<br /> <br /> Now, I agree with you that nothing about Elsewhere links back directly to Lunar thematics. But if they use it like either as a place to store things (that they steal like Ravens, or collect like squirrels or eat and it disappears like some Great White behemoth) or as a den (which connects many lands like a Rabbit's many burrows, or is warded by their scent/essence like the lair of some Beast out of hoary Lore), then I am about as okay with Lunars getting it, as Solars getting it.<br /> <br /> TL: DR If Solars can justify having Hammerspace, Lunars sure as heck can as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T00:28:52-08:00","id":1285142,"title":"","content":"Okay, you're arguing against a point I'm not making. The Elsewhere of 3e Solar charms is <b>not</b> a storage dimension like it was last edition and the book goes out of its way to explain this. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Elsewhere: Some Charms allow a character to send objects or equipment Elsewhere, defined categorically as someplace in existence that is not here. An object sent Elsewhere is inaccessible to everyone except whoever put it there. </div> </div> </div> We\u2019re going to see the return of an interdimensional lair in the native Lunar charmset on the weak justification it's kind of like what an animal does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T00:51:40-08:00","id":1285146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1285142#post1285142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, you're arguing against a point I'm not making. The Elsewhere of 3e Solar charms is <b>not</b> a storage dimension like it was last edition and the book goes out of its way to explain this. We\u2019re going to see the return of an interdimensional lair in the native Lunar charmset on the weak justification it's kind of like what an animal does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, fair enough. I am content with the bisected hair that we have achieved, so we'll just have to see the real thing next Tuesday then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:40:42-08:00","id":1285158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1285136#post1285136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Squirrel Girl doesn't store things in pocket dimensions.<br /> <br /> Even if she did, the argument that Lunars should because of that would be about as compelling as &amp;quot;Lunars should get nine lives because of Catwoman in Batman Returns&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure they were referencing the literal Squirrel Girl from Marvel and not just an ambiguous example of A Squirrel Girl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:44:43-08:00","id":1285159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1283462#post1283462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, the Kickstarter is overlapping with my child\u2019s due date... my partner will probably object to me dropping as much cash as I did on the DB Kickstarter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mozeltov! Hey I guess this is an excuse to name ones Offspring Fangs-at-the-Gate! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:57:52-08:00","id":1285163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284978#post1284978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I never actually saw anyone take those charms, so I'm not sure how they'd end up working in practice.<br /> <br /> Did any of you see them used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once.<br /> Secure Den Prana had a major problem common to MoEP: Lunars, where its essence rating was too high. By essence 4 running away from a potential fight is largely no longer part of the Circle's agenda unless they've ran into something like a Third Circle Demon.<br /> What makes it particularly bad was a comparison to the Shadowlands Circle spell Door of the Dead which can move a similar sized group back and forth between the Underworld and Creation. It wasn\u2019t as good but it was available at the point when you might actually want to run away from things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1284987#post1284987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Never. But I really liked the idea of Lunars being able to make some Wyld tricks. What I saw used were the mutiple action charms where one hit seemed to sprout from several different directions. That was a neat use of dimensional magic IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar Wyld tricks simply weren\u2019t worth it (Fair Folk hunting knacks not withstanding). Not when Graceful Wicked Masques provided everyone with a framework for acquiring Fair Folk Graces + charms.<br /> I tried using the Wyld keyworded Lunar charms but once I gained access to Wyld Stunting there was simply no going back for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-06-2019, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T19:15:26-08:00","id":1286344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1283533#post1283533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this the day we all waited for when Ex3 was first annouced?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, yes it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T21:50:57-08:00","id":1286361,"title":"","content":".......f4, f4, f4, f4, f4,f4, f4, f4,f4.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T23:57:42-08:00","id":1286374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1286361#post1286361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.......f4, f4, f4, f4, f4,f4, f4, f4,f4.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you don't mean F5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T17:05:34-08:00","id":1286581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1286374#post1286374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure you don't mean F5?</div> </div> </div> </div>......I don\u2019t usually use the function keys, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T23:57:40-08:00","id":1286631,"title":"","content":"It's strange to think that the Google Doc tabs containing previews from the last Kickstarter have been up continuously in my tab list for close to a year.<br /> <br /> I suppose... that this will be an appropriate time to finally retire them. :S<br /> <br /> This will likely have to be my most frugal Kickstarter, but I think I can make something work for it.<br /> <br /> More concerning is the matter of covering the book in my style. I cannot rely on my Microsoft Edge functioning with this forum anymore, and such lengthy write-ups are not well suited to being typed on my phone. I can think of only two alternatives; email them to myself so I can copy and paste them, or... actually, sounding out the alternative, it's too distasteful to me. That other one will do it.<br /> <br /> Unless... I post the same in full at RPG.Net and copy from there.<br /> <br /> ....Confound it, I could have done that with the What Fire Has Wrought art!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T01:26:31-08:00","id":1286642,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m trying to rein in the hype so that I\u2019m not all tuckered out come the day. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s hard, believe me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:53:35-08:00","id":1286703,"title":"","content":"Huh. It really does start tomorrow. Weird.<br /> <br /> I just bought a Nintendo Switch and two new games with some of the stolen money the IRS &quot;refunded&quot; to me, so this is awkward.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, only in terms of enthusiasm, not money. I still have more than enough spare money to back the Kickstarter, especially since I was never going to splurge for anything like &quot;new Charm or Artifact&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"