iner\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287169#post1287169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I note on this score that it's already passed WFHW, which funded in 2 hours. Some of that's probably the increased costs, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure also more trust from fans that the new devs will deliver on a timeline. I love DB so I was in there despite not having been totally resold on Exalted after a 2e burnout but I know a few people who still are stinging from the 3e KS delay. But DB came and was both great content and progressed in a fairly transparent and timely manner which is huge. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping this bodes well for future fatsplats too. More lore content in companions is my favorite new thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 02-12-2019, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T12:30:23-08:00","id":1287185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287147#post1287147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a youtube of the monologue video?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b99NNvfWe3g\" target=\"_blank\">Here we go.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T12:31:51-08:00","id":1287187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287185#post1287185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b99NNvfWe3g\" target=\"_blank\">Here we go.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>+1 Lunar XP<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T12:41:15-08:00","id":1287194,"title":"","content":"I really like the exaltation stories.<br /> <br /> So, a Lunar's essence fever gives them Unstoppable Rage.<br /> <br /> Interesting notes on the Moon-Touched<br /> <br /> Very good notes on Moon worship. It's highly individualized as appropriate for Luna. Very nice to see mortals worshiping her too. I wonder if the tea drunk by the Sisterhood has any magical properties. I like the Swiftest Rider in any case.<br /> <br /> No &quot;Prestige Splat&quot; pages here like in the DB book.<br /> <br /> Chapter 1 was really good, very nice overview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T12:47:36-08:00","id":1287200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lycaniz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287131#post1287131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its not 50 dollars outragerous.expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly it is. I ordered several packages last year before Christmas, 7 mangas and 2 BD 44$, 2 BD boxes 44$, 5 BD and 2 BD boxes 55$. It's not pretty, but not a lot that can be changed there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/47-lc1984","name":"LC1984","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar47_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T12:56:12-08:00","id":1287209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287194#post1287194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No &quot;Prestige Splat&quot; pages here like in the DB book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not doing prestige spreads just made more sense than trying to force them. We could have formalized the Sahan-ya schools more and given them to those, or like done one for the Silver Pact and one for the Shadow Fang Vanguard... but why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:03:40-08:00","id":1287210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287160#post1287160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> still a few limited slots open if you want something special.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but I put in some big money on both Core and Terrestrials, which are my favourites next to Sidereals. I'm gonna go basic on Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:17:50-08:00","id":1287214,"title":"","content":"I'm very happy to see that this KS is going so well. Thank you everyone for participating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:18:35-08:00","id":1287215,"title":"","content":"So, the post for the first part of the manuscript preview tells us that we'll be getting the chapters on Tuesdays and the charms on Fridays. Because there were so many that they had to be done separately.<br /> I'm speculating that this means we'll get the rules for Lunar charms, dicecaps, and keywords, plus Universal charms (which I assume to be few enough in number to fit) alongside one attribute this Friday. Then, every next Friday will have two attributes worth of charms. No idea if this is actually the case, but it would make sense?<br /> EDIT: Well, upon looking at my calendar again, it seems we only have four Fridays during the Kickstarter, so there's probably another way of splitting the charms that makes more sense. Looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8097,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","user":"wern212","date":". 02-12-2019, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:44:24-08:00","id":1287226,"title":"","content":"I find the idea of mixing up the order of the previews jarring personally. Makes more sense to me in order, even if people want to see mechanics sooner. Maybe I'm alone in that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:47:58-08:00","id":1287231,"title":"","content":"Chapter 2: The Silver Pact<br /> <br /> Hmmm.... the histories of those four luminaries are very interesting, offer a nice look at the difficulties faced by early Lunars, and a very nice insight as to why the Silver Pact is structured like it is.<br /> Really kind of a pity that there's no chance the Sids and Lunars could ever negotiate now, but ...Well with a number of leaders on both sides who remember the start of the war I doubt that was really possible.<br /> <br /> Cool stuff about the First Age. The Shadow Deliberative. The anti-authoritarian balance to the Second Deliberative. <br /> <br /> Ah, Politics. Everyone is equal in the Pact, but some are More Equal than others.<br /> <br /> Not entirely sure I like having to remember more new words, but ok, bring on the Silver Pact Jargon.<br /> <br /> So...theoretically, if you can get groupies, you can be a Shahan-ya, regardless of age? Is that right?<br /> <br /> Yeah, good note to remind everyone that, while they can be Loyal, no Lunar is &quot;Tame.&quot; Attempting to squash all dissent from your students is a good way to lose all your students.<br /> <br /> ....Ok, I first read that as Dances-Between-<i>Relationships</i> and I was wondering what one does to get<i> that</i> name.<br /> <br /> I like Gadhaj Winter-Wheel and I wish their agenda had gotten more traction. They went out with an awesome bang though! Hijacking a Thousand Forged Dragon is several kinds of awesome.<br /> <br /> ....I'm totally going to have a Lunar that, if Raksi's and Ma-Ha-Suchi's feud comes up, simply says &quot;they used to date.&quot;<br /> <br /> I really do like the way you're giving insight into the various stages of the Pact by giving us stories of prominent leaders at the time.<br /> <br /> I feel very sorry for any Lunar that tries to play peacemaker to this herd of cats.<br /> <br /> Just gonna note that Nahal is also used in the Stormlight Archive, to refer to a mystic bond between a human and a spirit. I have no idea if this is likely to be a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:51:43-08:00","id":1287233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287215#post1287215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the post for the first part of the manuscript preview tells us that we'll be getting the chapters on Tuesdays and the charms on Fridays. Because there were so many that they had to be done separately.<br /> I'm speculating that this means we'll get the rules for Lunar charms, dicecaps, and keywords, plus Universal charms (which I assume to be few enough in number to fit) alongside one attribute this Friday. Then, every next Friday will have two attributes worth of charms. No idea if this is actually the case, but it would make sense?<br /> EDIT: Well, upon looking at my calendar again, it seems we only have four Fridays during the Kickstarter, so there's probably another way of splitting the charms that makes more sense. Looking forward to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that part. Sounds neat! And kind of appropriate to mix things up for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:06:03-08:00","id":1287238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287231#post1287231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just gonna note that Nahal is also used in the Stormlight Archive, to refer to a mystic bond between a human and a spirit. I have no idea if this is likely to be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that both are derived from the Mesoamerican term nagual/nahual, so probably not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:13:59-08:00","id":1287241,"title":"","content":"Well, we are off to a good start in terms of reaching the goal. Lets see if we can do better then dragon blooded in terms of stretch goals this time. Not saying dragon blooded did bad to be clear, just saying lets try to be even more awesome then last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:31:09-08:00","id":1287254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287231#post1287231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...theoretically, if you can get groupies, you can be a Shahan-ya, regardless of age? Is that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the example Shahan-ya is only 100 years old, which as some of them are over 1500 years old, is relatively young.<br /> <br /> (Notice also that there are dozens of Shahan-ya. I find this interesting, as that means there's about 4-9 other Lunars per Shahan-Ya. Which is not tiny, but not a ton either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:38:24-08:00","id":1287255,"title":"","content":"I feel like lunars being this together feels odd. Even with the current situation at hand, non-sidereals have always had less issues killing each other in conflict. So I don't feel it's appropriate to have a situation where they have elders tell them to kiss and make up. Especially with how big creation is. Two lunars fighting and killing each other before other elders even know seems like a more likely situation but otherwise outside of a few issues I have, it looks fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:40:40-08:00","id":1287257,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Creation being this big means two Lunars who dislike each other are probably mostly going to avoid each other before it gets so bad they hate each other, and thus they're unlikely to kill each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:42:49-08:00","id":1287260,"title":"","content":"the art that has been showing are amazing, and I really love the text about the silver pact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:57:32-08:00","id":1287271,"title":"","content":"So I cannot parse this sentence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Whitewall, adherents of the Son-And-Daughter, a twin god-goddess forever standing back-to-back, reveal their true selves only under moonlight </div> </div> </div>Is this suggesting literally or metaphorically? Do they conceal their forms at all times? Is nudity only allowed under the moon? Do they conceal their personalities or other metaphor for 'true self' except under the light of the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:02:15-08:00","id":1287275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287257#post1287257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Creation being this big means two Lunars who dislike each other are probably mostly going to avoid each other before it gets so bad they hate each other, and thus they're unlikely to kill each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only issue is that Lunars feel like they should be much less structured than this. The structure makes creation feel a lot smaller than it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:02:17-08:00","id":1287276,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that the basic age-groups of the Lunar Exalted are finally given some real attention this time, and only an appropriate amount of it.<br /> <br /> Taking the concept of &quot;barbarism&quot; out behind the shed and shooting it is also welcomed.<br /> <br /> I love Kinslayer's idea of finding a rich asshole in the Threshold, killing them, and using their house and wealth to serve her hospitality for a meeting with other Lunars. The comedy of all these mortals mingling with Lunars unawares writes itself. Also the horror stories of mortal servants and guests wandering into the wrong room, or bumping into the worst cannibal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:08:50-08:00","id":1287283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287275#post1287275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only issue is that Lunars feel like they should be much less structured than this. The structure makes creation feel a lot smaller than it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's far less than 2nd ed. But I do agree with you a little (I mean, I don't think they need to be much less structured, but a little would be fine. Or rather, make it more clear that Lunars in the West don't interact with those in the East, etc)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I appreciate that the basic age-groups of the Lunar Exalted are finally given some real attention this time,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that needed to be considered and hasn't been until now.<br /> <br /> I liked the way they talked about how weird and disconnected the First Age Lunars are, so that generally it's actually the Shogunate-era Lunars who are really the Elders in practice. And this was born out with stuff like Ul of the Burning Eye and Sha's Oka.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Taking the concept of &quot;barbarism&quot; out behind the shed and shooting it is also welcomed. </div> </div> </div>But they get D12 hit points! And more interesting skills than Fighters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:14:32-08:00","id":1287287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287283#post1287283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's far less than 2nd ed. But I do agree with you a little (I mean, I don't think they need to be much less structured, but a little would be fine. Or rather, make it more clear that Lunars in the West don't interact with those in the East, etc)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I think that it should be a lot less looser is because they have wildly conflicting ideals to get to the same goal more than that it also feels like young lunars are automatically beholden to older lunars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:18:50-08:00","id":1287293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287276#post1287276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love Kinslayer's idea of finding a rich asshole in the Threshold, killing them, and using their house and wealth to serve her hospitality for a meeting with other Lunars. The comedy of all these mortals mingling with Lunars unawares writes itself. Also the horror stories of mortal servants and guests wandering into the wrong room, or bumping into the worst cannibal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, someone draw Raksi politely talking with a group of Dynasts with Moonsilver Grocho Marx glasses on? Pleeeease?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:44:33-08:00","id":1287311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287283#post1287283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that needed to be considered and hasn't been until now.<br /> <br /> I liked the way they talked about how weird and disconnected the First Age Lunars are, so that generally it's actually the Shogunate-era Lunars who are really the Elders in practice. And this was born out with stuff like Ul of the Burning Eye and Sha's Oka.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also love the fresh new look into the mindset of the Shogunate Lunars and the Contagion Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:14:39-08:00","id":1287317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287283#post1287283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather, make it more clear that Lunars in the West don't interact with those in the East, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's not coming across clearly, we'll see if it's possible to tweak the wording for more clarity after editing. There is some interaction between distant Lunars, but most interaction is local, and most individual Lunar activity is effectively independent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:23:04-08:00","id":1287322,"title":"","content":"I really love their whole structure of governing themselves. It's ad-hoc everything, totally immune to the rigid and brittle hierarchy of the Realm, but still moving as one groundswelling wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:30:03-08:00","id":1287325,"title":"","content":"We have broken past 100K","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:34:50-08:00","id":1287327,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, I <i>loooove</i> the new Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi is completely different, but I like him as a grumpy old veteran who may or may not have an overly nostalgic view of the First Age even if he wants something rather different in theory and practice way better than a generic hentai villain. Meanwhile, Raksi has been changed little, other than that she's <i>perfectly effing sane.</i> This makes her both far more sympathetic (because while she's still a monster, she's a very <i>human </i>monster who desperately wants to avenge her people and friends while not making the same mistakes the Realm did and does), and far more terrifying (because her tyrannical hedonism is an <i>entirely deliberate </i>way to intimidate and entice; she's not a decadent, she's a ruthlessly competent politician and sorceress who simply parties as hard as she works, and with just as much concern for those in the way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:48:08-08:00","id":1287331,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda sad there's no Generation Zero left, even if I get why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:51:37-08:00","id":1287334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287331#post1287331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda sad there's no Generation Zero left, even if I get why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, that's amazing fodder for an ST to introduce into a game. The players know there's none left, the characters certainly do, but then when you find one sleeping under a great mountain in the east...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:01:24-08:00","id":1287338,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, and I'm guessing Essence Fever is what they're calling Lunar Limit now.<br /> <br /> This is an unmitigated improvement. It even ties into how obsessive the Silver Pact is; there's a flaw in the very Exaltation that makes them prone to holding grudges and acting on them. A Lunar is very much an outsider and trickster hero; hurt her, and she <i>remembers.</i> Especially since that for the Lunars, the Great Curse was a <i>mixed blessing. </i>Yes, they do get intense about revenge, but the rage is fed by things that have truly hurt them in the past and is completely under their control; it can be focused, tamed, turned into something good, it just can't ever burn out. So, they don't see it as a problem, or if they do, it's one they've made peace with, shrugging and politely sweeping one of them having a bad day (read here: foaming at the mouth, declaring oaths of eternal hatred, screaming berserk fury, usually at the same time) under the rug to deal with the fallout later.<br /> <br /> I am seriously hoping we get mechanics that build Essence Fever for benefits, in other words (&quot;I AM TOO PISSED OFF TO LISTEN TO PALTRY DESTINY AND PROPHECY, PUNY SIDEREAL!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-12-2019, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:03:45-08:00","id":1287340,"title":"","content":"Solars and Dragon-Blooded also get Essence Fever, with descriptions of it in their respective first chapters. It's not something with mechanics for those two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:06:32-08:00","id":1287344,"title":"","content":"Finally had a chance to finish reading the preview so far, loving it so far. Its nice to finally see elders who aren't first age level ancient in positions of leadership. Something in specific I'm interested in seeing further fleshed out is the reference to the fact that they were the best necromancers around for most of the second age. Hopefully that means they get second circle necromancy this edition (assuming its still split into 3 levels like sorcery by the time they get around to publishing necromancy stuff). It was always pretty lame that nobody but solars and abyssals were allowed access to second circle necromancy without having to go find a grave goods mantle of Brigid devoted to necromancy or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> I do vaguely remember there eventually being a lunar charm in 2ed that let them get it in exchange for giving up their ability to use second circle sorcery but I can't remember if that was official errata or a custom charm I read somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:08:03-08:00","id":1287345,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Assassination tidbit is odd given how several of the mentioned NPCs are described / implied as having done just that (though, I guess not to Dynasts?) Is the point of it to answer the question of why DBs aren't constantly worried about shapeshifting assassins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:13:21-08:00","id":1287347,"title":"","content":"Its not like it says that they <i>never</i> do it, just that they do it sparingly because doing it too often is a good way to get a bunch of wyld hunts unleashed in the area and makes potential targets in that general area really paranoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:38:34-08:00","id":1287355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287338#post1287338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, and I'm guessing Essence Fever is what they're calling Lunar Limit now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to rain on your parade, but no, Lunar Limit is separate, and still called that as far as I know. &quot;Essence fever&quot; is a term used for most Exalted, it represents that tendency of new Exalts to go out and get things done, trample jeweled thrones beneath their sandled feet, shakes the pillars of Heaven, etc. It's referenced in the Core book as something most Exalts of all types go through (pp. 35-36). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:50:47-08:00","id":1287359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287344#post1287344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally had a chance to finish reading the preview so far, loving it so far. Its nice to finally see elders who aren't first age level ancient in positions of leadership. Something in specific I'm interested in seeing further fleshed out is the reference to the fact that they were the best necromancers around for most of the second age. Hopefully that means they get second circle necromancy this edition (assuming its still split into 3 levels like sorcery by the time they get around to publishing necromancy stuff).</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. <span style=\"color:white\">10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:52:54-08:00","id":1287360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287359#post1287359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bingo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, they finally get to be 2 up 2 down like they always should've been rather than 2/1 because solars? I should be way less excited to hear that than I am, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:13:10-08:00","id":1287366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287359#post1287359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bingo. <span style=\"color:white\">10char</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That made my day, really happy they can manage that now. Definitely want to run a no moon necromancer at some point. Seems like a good thing to go with their boundary hopping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:17:27-08:00","id":1287369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287345#post1287345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Assassination tidbit is odd given how several of the mentioned NPCs are described / implied as having done just that (though, I guess not to Dynasts?) Is the point of it to answer the question of why DBs aren't constantly worried about shapeshifting assassins?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually brought this up exactly in a thread a couple of months ago. Lunar shapeshifting, combined with the fact that they're second only to Solars in raw power, makes living when they don't want you to a seemingly insurmountable task. In theory a Lunar could circle around the Threshold as a bird just picking off vulnerable Dynasts at their leisure. In their palanquin as they parade through the city, in their bed while they're sleeping, or even when they're sitting on the good old chamberpot. Even if you have half a dozen mortal guards with you at all times they're just chaff to be winnowed before celestial might.<br /> <br /> So you either need to have decent reasons why Lunars are reluctant to do that to an enemy that they positively drip with hatred for, have them constantly do it and wonder how the Realm functions when it's constantly having high ranking leaders killed, or have to start writing Dynasts like death awaits outside every open window and make them hide their identity from the public and live in fortified bunkers ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:37:15-08:00","id":1287378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287360#post1287360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, they finally get to be 2 up 2 down like they always should've been rather than 2/1 because solars? I should be way less excited to hear that than I am, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can access both Celestial Circle Sorcery and [REDACTED] Circle Necromancy at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:39:27-08:00","id":1287379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287378#post1287378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can access both Celestial Circle Sorcery and [REDACTED] Circle Necromancy at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we have a Redacted Circle as a kickstarter stretch goal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:50:31-08:00","id":1287382,"title":"","content":"Will we actually be getting some necromancy in the lunar book I wonder?<br /> <br /> <br /> So, who is every bodies favorite new lunar from the previews so far? I like the kin slayer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T20:26:28-08:00","id":1287404,"title":"","content":"Lunar Generations<br /> <br /> Yeah....it's weird to think that, for many of these people, their only real Non-Lunar peers are ....Well, Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Ok, so four generations<br /> <br /> Third generation....ouch. That's rough. I can imagine that many of them are starting to go &quot;Oh crap, it's happening again!&quot; these days.<br /> <br /> Really, all these short bits on Lunar elders are cool.<br /> <br /> Second Generation: The Realm is easy mode compared to the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> First Generation: these guys are all probably crazy, aren't they? They're the dragons in their caves, sphinxes in the wild, and so on. I think it works. <br /> <br /> The fact that they have probably had naps that lasted longer than the Shogunate is kind of scary.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure that outlawing Generation Zero was necessary.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hello, I'm from the Silver Pact and I'd like to give you a no-pressure invitation to join. Here's a pamphlet and my card. If it sounds interesting you can come to a few meetings and see what you think.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunting new Solars is suddenly starting to sound much easier than new Lunars.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T20:35:34-08:00","id":1287406,"title":"","content":"So... Shahan-ya is now specifically Old Realm. It might have been before, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> There's also a Pact Argot section.<br /> <br /> Is there room for an Old Realm linguistics project? Is Old Realm overlapping with First Tongue?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I may not have gotten that far, but is there a description why dissolving and reforming the castes was beneficial?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T21:05:01-08:00","id":1287412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287406#post1287406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Shahan-ya is now specifically Old Realm. It might have been before, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> There's also a Pact Argot section.<br /> <br /> Is there room for an Old Realm linguistics project? Is Old Realm overlapping with First Tongue?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I may not have gotten that far, but is there a description why dissolving and reforming the castes was beneficial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think anything released so far mentions what exactly the benefit was in altering their castes like they did. But I'm sure it will definitely be better then 'they hung out in the wyld doing nothing for so long the wyld exposure melted their exaltations and the modern castes were all they could salvage when stabilizing them'. If it goes into detail I'd imagine it will be in the character creation section where they give an overview of the castes and the general activities usually done by a generic member of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T21:41:00-08:00","id":1287416,"title":"","content":"Oh, man, another PDF where all the bookmarks are automatically open.<br /> <br /> The corebook wasn't so bad about this because at least each individual Charm didn't get its own bookmark, but the Dragon-Blooded pdf does and it makes scrolling through the bookmarks window a chore. I just want to jump to a particular Ability; I can find an individual Charm on my own.<br /> <br /> Chapter Bookmarks should definitely start closed, though I do find it helpful to have all sub-chapter bookmarks open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T22:00:05-08:00","id":1287425,"title":"","content":"The boundary of monstrosity and humanity that Lunars can cross seems to apply to the perceptions of others, too.<br /> <br /> Raksi puts on a show of being a monster, while being a much more sane and companiable creature in truth. Of course, she's still a cold-hearted monster willing to feed live babies to other Lunars as a test and distraction, but she can probably go in reverse to smooth over memories of her monstrosity with a mask of humanity.<br /> <br /> While people can misunderstand others all on their own, Ma-Ha-Suchi might be employing deliberate subterfuge with his own followers, at least to prevent Kathaka from noticing his condescending sentiments. He's definitely hiding his intent to turn Ranotis against his father for his own benefit, though he may fooling Ranotis into thinking he's warmer inside than he seems to others. He's definitely invested in keeping people from really getting to know himself, since Anja's lack of interest in his feelings is actually a plus for him.<br /> <br /> Sha'a Oka is a completely different person in person than in public.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T23:19:04-08:00","id":1287435,"title":"","content":"So, Favor trading is complicated, but it sounds pretty similar to a lot of the ways pre-industrial societies and/or small villages handled things.<br /> <br /> The Shahan-ya Councils are where they ratify the decisions of the executive officer of the week I see. I assume most need to be ratified by a simple majority in the case of purely internal affairs, but by a two thirds majority in the case of more major- &quot;Be Quiet! I order you to be quiet!&quot;<br /> <br /> So, she murders a dude, takes over their wealth, and uses it to hold a banquet? That's hella creepy, right? Right?<br /> <br /> I like the prohibition against murder, but I imagine that it could be difficult to prove at times. ....Though, now I'm imagining a newly Exalted Lunar who has called council to accuse another Lunar of the murder of their previous life. That could be interesting.<br /> <br /> I do like that they don't just exile people and hope that it solves the problem.<br /> <br /> The Realm is horrible. However, there are times when it is horribly useful, because they do actually solve problems with rogue gods, bandits, Fae, and other such problems. But the system is still terrible and uncaring and, worst of all, makes other national leaders go &quot;Hey, I wanna be like THAT!&quot; and perpetuates itself.<br /> <br /> Good points on why assassination is a relatively rare thing. I enjoy the idea of Dynasts using Doppleganger Codes.<br /> <br /> ...Lunars undermine attempts at reform, presumably on the basis that it'd be &quot;too little, too late,&quot; because none of the Dynasts really want to give up their ability to do lines of jade infused coke off a pleasure slave's belly. But, that got me wondering about what Creation might look like today if the remnants of the Lunars and Sids had come together during the Fae invasion and/or the bit just after when Her Redness claimed Creation and they all tried to rebuild everything? Can you imagine a Realm where the DBs serve as monster hunters and basically do what they do now, but the Lunars are there to counter balance things, so the Realm doesn't take too much? Where neither side has to pour all this extra energy into fighting each other? Where the Wyld Hunt doesn't exist (so, yes, there's like ten living Solars. If one of them really does go crazy, we thin we can probably handle that.)<br /> <br /> I get that all the bad blood made trust impossible and so that could never be ...and that makes me very sad.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the best ways to kill the Realm<br /> <br /> Herding cats again.<br /> <br /> Guerilla road workers, who show up and rip up roads in the middle of the night. Ninja accountants who sneak in and alter tax records.<br /> <br /> Also, now I'm thinking about Fight Club and a group of Lunars and humans who attempt to burn down the main records building in the Realm. I could actually see some great houses helping with that, since you could just say &quot;Debt? What debt? No-one has any way to prove I haven't paid you, especially since I have records here that say I did. So are we done here?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;....Wait, let me get this straight. We're fighting imperialism and your main plan for combating this is, basically, to force them to make the imperialism worse?&quot; &quot;Yup!&quot; &quot;Really?!?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, house cat vs. Mouse!Lunar who really doesn't want to give anything away is totally a thing that should happen in games and more Guild Factors should be carrying insect eating animals on their shoulders, got it.<br /> <br /> Someone acting weird and then vanishing is a pretty solid sign of Lunar activity. It wouldn't surprise me if some Lunars didn't arrange to do that periodically just to heighten paranoia. Or even get some mortals to fake it for them.<br /> <br /> Oooh, yeah. I have always loved the idea that you can sneak into a manse, rearrange the furniture, and then it explodes a week later, and I will be looking forward to rules for that in 3e. But, yeah, tricking the Realm into walking their forces through an ancient Working that even you barely understand also sounds hella fun.<br /> <br /> I keep thinking about how, if you had half the hearthstones in the corebook together, they could enrich and protect a small city state. You might need to move them around a bit sometimes, but it could be pretty idyllic there. I could see a Lunar doing this.<br /> <br /> Yeah I could see Lunars faced with the prospect of trying to assemble a professional, open field army balking because they know exactly how vulnerable such large and slow targets are and how expensive they are to maintain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-13-2019, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T23:52:15-08:00","id":1287442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287435#post1287435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, she murders a dude, takes over their wealth, and uses it to hold a banquet? That's hella creepy, right? Right?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;....Wait, let me get this straight. We're fighting imperialism and your main plan for combating this is, basically, to force them to make the imperialism worse?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Yup!&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Really?!?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah these are two of the kind of subtle ways that the book implies that Lunars are not always the most pure heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T00:16:12-08:00","id":1287444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287317#post1287317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's not coming across clearly, we'll see if it's possible to tweak the wording for more clarity after editing. There is some interaction between distant Lunars, but most interaction is local, and most individual Lunar activity is effectively independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are parts where it is clear, or at least the distances are considered (for example, 2 Lunar Elders who communicate via Infallible Messenger and who've never met). But other parts have Shahan-Ya who seem to be interacting between Directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T00:23:53-08:00","id":1287446,"title":"","content":"I really liked the history section; it felt like a process, not just a jump from the Primordial War to the High First Age to today, in terms of characters.<br /> There are characters Exalted at all different times, including some famous ones who are dead. I don't think 2nd ed had any famous dead Lunars except Ingosh Silver-Claws. <br /> <br /> It's also good that each Shahan-Ya described comes with a team, they're not just alone.<br /> <br /> But I was a bit disappointed that, unlike those mentioned in the Core book, almost none of them tell you what their spirit shape is. But that's fundamental to understanding a Lunar's character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T00:50:47-08:00","id":1287450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287446#post1287446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I was a bit disappointed that, unlike those mentioned in the Core book, almost none of them tell you what their spirit shape is. But that's fundamental to understanding a Lunar's character.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be that's for Chapter 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T00:57:43-08:00","id":1287451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287444#post1287444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are parts where it is clear, or at least the distances are considered (for example, 2 Lunar Elders who communicate via Infallible Messenger and <b>who've never met</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm admittedly AFB at the moment, but isn't a requirement of Infallible Messenger that you know who you're sending it to?<br /> <br /> I admittedly could be misremembering; it's just that the alternative seems pretty abusable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T01:03:26-08:00","id":1287452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287451#post1287451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm admittedly AFB at the moment, but isn't a requirement of Infallible Messenger that you know who you're sending it to?<br /> <br /> I admittedly could be misremembering; it's just that the alternative seems pretty abusable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checked and... nope! (Only reference is to \u201ctarget character\u201d, appropriate given this use)<br /> <br /> Time to DDOS the Scarlet Empress!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T01:40:22-08:00","id":1287455,"title":"","content":"Does it work on someone when you don't know their name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T01:48:14-08:00","id":1287456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287455#post1287455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it work on someone when you don't know their name?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire spell description does not contain one instance of the word \u201cname\u201d or any synonyms I was able to decipher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T03:11:33-08:00","id":1287471,"title":"","content":"That said, given the way the Empress feels about those who'd treat with her, there's every possibility that she's done some sort of Working to stymie Infallible Messengers or punish those who send them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T03:21:11-08:00","id":1287472,"title":"","content":"I had a player once who kept wanting to send infallible messengers to the Empress (V'neef in my game). My explanation for why that was a bad idea was that the Empress was warded against that kind of sorcery, forcing messages to be sent to underlings unless she had specifically allowed certain sorcerers direct access. Other people may have different explanations, but that's what I felt make sense for my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:22:37-08:00","id":1287489,"title":"","content":"So. <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2415113\" target=\"_blank\">It seems Silent Pearl's a Shogunate survivor, at the very least</a>. The DBs and Alchemicals have both had centuries-old sigs, but I think this makes Silent Pearl the first Lunar/Sidereal sig confirmed to have lived that long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:25:55-08:00","id":1287562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287435#post1287435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;....Wait, let me get this straight. We're fighting imperialism and your main plan for combating this is, basically, to force them to make the imperialism worse?&quot; &quot;Yup!&quot; &quot;Really?!?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this really highlights a nice aspect of the Lunar lore this edition (I'm not sure how much this is different from prior incarnations). The Lunars aren't fighting Imperialism, they're fighting an Empire. Ma-Ha-Suchi (and many others) just wants to replace who gets to sit on the throne. <br /> <br /> When you're fighting an empire, you get to cloak your rhetoric in anti-imperialist rhetoric, but making imperialism <i>worse</i> to mobilize a conquered population is too effective a strategy to ignore. I'm sure there are some Lunars who are genuinely fighting to improve the lots of the people, but even some of those genuine idealists will still be willing to sacrifice those alive today (or yesterday or tomorrow) for the benefit of future generations.<br /> <br /> After all, if you can prod the Realm into atrocity, aren't its victims martyrs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T10:26:53-08:00","id":1287577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287562#post1287562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this really highlights a nice aspect of the Lunar lore this edition (I'm not sure how much this is different from prior incarnations). The Lunars aren't fighting Imperialism, they're fighting an Empire. Ma-Ha-Suchi (and many others) just wants to replace who gets to sit on the throne. <br /> <br /> When you're fighting an empire, you get to cloak your rhetoric in anti-imperialist rhetoric, but making imperialism <i>worse</i> to mobilize a conquered population is too effective a strategy to ignore. I'm sure there are some Lunars who are genuinely fighting to improve the lots of the people, but even some of those genuine idealists will still be willing to sacrifice those alive today (or yesterday or tomorrow) for the benefit of future generations.<br /> <br /> After all, if you can prod the Realm into atrocity, aren't its victims martyrs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think that, once again, this give a great space for PCs to play in. With PCs who are legit idealists, who\u2019s problem with the Realm isn\u2019t just that they\u2019re not the ones on top. They can come to the realization that not every shahan-ya imbittered by centuries of war shares those ideals. Even if your shahan-ya does, you have to balance how much you\u2019re willing to sacrifice to work with the others. <br /> <br /> Then when they decide to transition to open war you start see the same kind of atrocities being committed by your allies. Do you decide that the wisdom of your elders must be right, and this is the only way? Or do you risk fighting amongst others in your cause, at precisely the time that your forces are most vulnerable to the Realm\u2019s brand of power. Or put up with it until the Realm is broken, and then make your move to stop the Silver Realm from replacing the Jade one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T11:53:45-08:00","id":1287612,"title":"","content":"So, how many people do you think know about Burning Eye's plan to make a second great plague? I feel like thats the kind of thing that makes a bunch of other lunars say 'WTF bro, are you crazy!?' if they knew he was tampering with that kind of thing (even if his intent is to make it specifically targeted in the end). From the sound of it lots of lunars might complain even if they thought it was possible to safely mess with that kind of thing because they don't want to kill <i>all</i> dragon blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:49:59-08:00","id":1287682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287612#post1287612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how many people do you think know about Burning Eye's plan to make a second great plague? I feel like thats the kind of thing that makes a bunch of other lunars say 'WTF bro, are you crazy!?' if they knew he was tampering with that kind of thing (even if his intent is to make it specifically targeted in the end). From the sound of it lots of lunars might complain even if they thought it was possible to safely mess with that kind of thing because they don't want to kill <i>all</i> dragon blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that most would oppose it, once you realize just how bat-shit insane it is. He's not targeting the Exalted directly, he's targeting &quot;Everyone who shares the Dragon's blood.&quot; He wants to wipe out <i>anyone</i> that has a dragon-blooded ancestor, no matter how distant. It's genocide on a massive scale. He'd depopulate the Blessed Isle, the Scavenger Lands. It's, well, lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:48:21-08:00","id":1287717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287682#post1287682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that most would oppose it, once you realize just how bat-shit insane it is. He's not targeting the Exalted directly, he's targeting &quot;Everyone who shares the Dragon's blood.&quot; He wants to wipe out <i>anyone</i> that has a dragon-blooded ancestor, no matter how distant. It's genocide on a massive scale. He'd depopulate the Blessed Isle, the Scavenger Lands. It's, well, lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably tear open lots of Shadowlands, for one thing.<br /> <br /> It could theoretically be major enough to stir the Five Elemental Dragons from their slumber.<br /> <br /> It would leave Creation without a major force for order and protection against the Underworld, Wyld, stray demons, and abusive gods.<br /> <br /> It would even kill some Lunars and family of Lunars, like Amantha Kinslayer and her Terrestrial descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:56:15-08:00","id":1287722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287612#post1287612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how many people do you think know about Burning Eye's plan to make a second great plague? I feel like thats the kind of thing that makes a bunch of other lunars say 'WTF bro, are you crazy!?' if they knew he was tampering with that kind of thing (even if his intent is to make it specifically targeted in the end). From the sound of it lots of lunars might complain even if they thought it was possible to safely mess with that kind of thing because they don't want to kill <i>all</i> dragon blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's supposed to be targeting the Dragon-Blooded proper. It'll be addressed in post-editing development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:52:50-08:00","id":1287779,"title":"","content":"I see that there are four martial arts up as a stretch goal for the companion book. Do we have any information regarding what martial arts (If any) are in Fangs at the gate? I seem to recall reading that there was a falcon style but, I can't recall where I would have read that and it's a sufficiently vague recollection that it could be my memory playing tricks on me.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see that, according to the text we have, chapter seven of the book &quot;offers several unique new Martial Arts styles&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T18:25:15-08:00","id":1287785,"title":"","content":"Falcon Style, Centipede Style, Swaying Grass Style, and Laughing Monster Styles are confirmed for Lunars: Fangs At The Gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T18:29:46-08:00","id":1287786,"title":"","content":"4 additional Animal Styles we\u2019ve never seen in previous editions in the Companion (Frog, Monkey, Bear, and Rat) was not something I expected but am very excited for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedb