quo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287975#post1287975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that was accomplished by splitting hybrid form and DBT stat boosts from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... thought that's what I said? Maybe not? I dunno!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T10:10:07-08:00","id":1287982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287962#post1287962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026 that reminds me. Are there rules in the Social System for making someone believe <i>you</i> have an Intimacy that you do not, in fact, have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think directly, but what you can do is role play it one way and have great guile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T10:25:24-08:00","id":1287985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287981#post1287981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I... thought that's what I said? Maybe not? I dunno!</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Elfive is refering to the fact that in Eska of the Seven Blades' statblock, her write-up of HBT has a duration of instant. In the new charm text, it appears as Indefinite, meaning the motes would be committed for the duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T10:58:41-08:00","id":1287998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287985#post1287985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Elfive is refering to the fact that in Eska of the Seven Blades' statblock, her write-up of HBT has a duration of instant. In the new charm text, it appears as Indefinite, meaning the motes would be committed for the duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, if that's the case than ignore me. I missed that detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T10:58:50-08:00","id":1287999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287982#post1287982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think directly, but what you can do is role play it one way and have great guile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I think a Charm (under Socialize) for almost any Exalt (at varying power levels) should be a Reflexive Charm upon someone failing to Read Intentions that makes them think that the Read Intentions succeeds with a result under the Exalt's control. This seems like such a useful ability that it's odd that I haven't seen anything like this yet.<br /> <br /> Although Sidereals having this would be... interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:29:14-08:00","id":1288008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287788#post1287788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it's awesome! It's not even Lunar exclusive either, Solars, DBs, anyone can use them. it's candy for everyone. I'm excited to see Bear, like way too excited...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious how brutal-grappling focused Bear Style will be made distinct enough from Solar Brawl to be worth the investment for Solars. We will see!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:45:58-08:00","id":1288017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287999#post1287999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but I think a Charm (under Socialize) for almost any Exalt (at varying power levels) should be a Reflexive Charm upon someone failing to Read Intentions that makes them think that the Read Intentions succeeds with a result under the Exalt's control. This seems like such a useful ability that it's odd that I haven't seen anything like this yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Solars <i>do</i> have something <i>like</i> that. Three, even. One lets the Solar socialite pass himself off as useless, someone to be disregarded; one lets the Solar socialite pass himself off as useful, the key to getting that thing the attempted reader needs; the third lets the Solar socialite pass himself off as a void of infinite depth that leaves his attempted reader hypnotized.<br /> <br /> There's not a Charm that lets you pretend a Read Intentions roll against you succeeded because Read Intentions rolls don't exist in-character. The only people who know a Read Intentions roll succeeded or failed are the players, and if doesn't foster a good gaming environment for a Charm to have you lie to your fellow players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-14-2019, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:01:23-08:00","id":1288021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1288008#post1288008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm curious how brutal-grappling focused Bear Style will be made distinct enough from Solar Brawl to be worth the investment for Solars. We will see!</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is less emphasis on throwing and more on gaining soak and/or health levels. Thick skin, thick fur, and brutal crushing grapples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:17:23-08:00","id":1288026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1288017#post1288017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Solars <i>do</i> have something <i>like</i> that. Three, even. One lets the Solar socialite pass himself off as useless, someone to be disregarded; one lets the Solar socialite pass himself off as useful, the key to getting that thing the attempted reader needs; the third lets the Solar socialite pass himself off as a void of infinite depth that leaves his attempted reader hypnotized.<br /> <br /> There's not a Charm that lets you pretend a Read Intentions roll against you succeeded because Read Intentions rolls don't exist in-character. The only people who know a Read Intentions roll succeeded or failed are the players, and if doesn't foster a good gaming environment for a Charm to have you lie to your fellow players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enh. I don't find your argument about the 'in-character / out-character' issue persuasive. All because the mechanics of such a Charm would allow you to invert the expectation of Read Intentions (and I would restrict it to that), that doesn't mean that that is how the in-character narrative plays out.<br /> <br /> I do find your argument about lying to fellow players persuasive, though. I should point out that my players tend to be <i>much</i> more cohesive and not worried about other players knowing their Intimacies, but I can see how other groups that are not so focused would have issue.<br /> <br /> I'll just use an example to help make sure we are on the same page about this. Imagine a character saying/thinking, 'Wow, this guy is really going off on an anti-Immaculate screed. Does he really hate the Immaculates so much?' That is easily an in-story concept that is, mechanically, asking for Read Intentions. The answers you can normally get is either the truth or, 'you can't tell/don't know'. 'You don't know' is a <i>very</i> different animal than believing a lie. And pulling social antagonists into false positions where they try to Persuade you using an Intimacy <i>you don't actually have</i> would be an awesome defensive tool, reserving your precious Willpower for more important issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:26:58-08:00","id":1288034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1288026#post1288026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enh. I don't find your argument about the 'in-character / out-character' issue persuasive. All because the mechanics of such a Charm would allow you to invert the expectation of Read Intentions (and I would restrict it to that), that doesn't mean that that is how the in-character narrative plays out.<br /> <br /> I do find your argument about lying to fellow players persuasive, though. I should point out that my players tend to be <i>much</i> more cohesive and not worried about other players knowing their Intimacies, but I can see how other groups that are not so focused would have issue.<br /> <br /> I'll just use an example to help make sure we are on the same page about this. Imagine a character saying/thinking, 'Wow, this guy is really going off on an anti-Immaculate screed. Does he really hate the Immaculates so much?' That is easily an in-story concept that is, mechanically, asking for Read Intentions. The answers you can normally get is either the truth or, 'you can't tell/don't know'. 'You don't know' is a <i>very</i> different animal than believing a lie. And pulling social antagonists into false positions where they try to Persuade you using an Intimacy <i>you don't actually have</i> would be an awesome defensive tool, reserving your precious Willpower for more important issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, this makes me wonder if a failed RI roll is even supposed to give you the information that you can\u2019t tell. Is it possible that a failed roll just returns \u201cyep, he doesn\u2019t appear to be hiding anything. What you see is what you get.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:32:09-08:00","id":1288037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1288034#post1288034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, this makes me wonder if a failed RI roll is even supposed to give you the information that you can\u2019t tell. Is it possible that a failed roll just returns \u201cyep, he doesn\u2019t appear to be hiding anything. What you see is what you get.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. 'WYSIWYG', out of character, equals 'You don't know'. Of course, social masters manipulate their opponents even when the opponents succeed.<br /> <br /> Player: &quot;I'm going on a huge anti-Immaculate screed at this satrapial reception.'<br /> ST: &quot;Okay, many people are looking at you wondering whether you're crazy or if you indeed hold that position.' Read Intentions.<br /> Player: &quot;Yeah, I'm not resisting that. I have no Intimacy towards the Immaculates.'<br /> ST: &quot;Okay... so now people are treating you like a troll.' (Internet version, obv)<br /> Player: &quot;Good. Now they're likely to underestimate me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T03:46:59-08:00","id":1288217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1287941#post1287941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, that's too bad. I kind of liked the notion of a First Age Elder who was so twisted by centuries of hate that he looked at a second Nine-Fold Decimation as a good plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't mean you can't do it.<br /> An observation I had with the Dragon-Blooded book that remains true here, there's an apparent desire to avoid presenting situations that were practically the default expectation of previous editions such as the elder exalt with a plan that's so insane that stopping it at the eleventh hour is the only real way you can interact with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T04:15:57-08:00","id":1288219,"title":"","content":"What did people think of the previewed charms?<br /> I was surprised that HBR gave 6 dots, and not X+Y dots, but I think it's better that way. A flat cost means you don't have to change it later, and it's not like having 6 dots of mutations at Essence 1 is broken.<br /> <br /> I also liked Chimera Soul-Expression, as you could use it to have a totem like a Gryphon or Coatl or something.<br /> <br /> As the others were 3 Appearance charms and 1 Charisma charm,I'm guessing it's the social Attribute charms that being released today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T04:19:17-08:00","id":1288221,"title":"","content":"I've said elsewhere that Hybrid Body is difficult to assess right now with the corebook's offerings for supernatural merits. If we've got good mutations it'll be great, otherwise growing wings the main appeal I see of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T05:07:43-08:00","id":1288223,"title":"","content":"Well, there's soak, enhanced senses (which are pricey, but are non-charm), poison, etc.<br /> But they're not amazing, I guess (though the soak is good for someone doing unarmoured martial arts). I see your point about the merits in the Lunar book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T05:40:38-08:00","id":1288229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1288223#post1288223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(though the soak is good for someone doing unarmoured martial arts).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the reverse personally, the mutations are supposed to reflect your spirit shape so at the 4-5 points of soak level Unusual Hide is a carapace or bone armour. I mean, yeah you could be a Ninja Turtle but the charmset is probably going to reward you for being a stamina focused soakbeast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:29:40-08:00","id":1288240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2416527\" target=\"_blank\">Charm preview's up for backers</a>, covering Excellencies, Universal, Appearance and Charisma Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:10:51-08:00","id":1288262,"title":"","content":"The timing's a bit awkward; it's hard to judge the shapeshifting Charms without knowing the rest of the rules. They look very... clean, I guess? The options for customizing spirit shapes are great and I really like Many-Faced Moon Transformation. It's a small, but extremely practical thing. <br /> <br /> I've just started on the Appearance Charms and so far, I absolutely love how they leverage the Influence mechanics for unique effects that fit Lunars very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:45:50-08:00","id":1288273,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've almost finished the Appearance charms, and I like them a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:50:42-08:00","id":1288275,"title":"","content":"I love the Universal Charms. We don't have the full view, yet, but even the incomplete picture looks great. I didn't even imagine that Many-Faced Moon Transformation would be a Universal Charm, but it's so much better than making it an Appearance or Manipulation Charm. It's not a &quot;Changing Moon&quot; Charm, it's a &quot;Lunar&quot; Charm like I never fully understood I wanted!<br /> <br /> My one complaint is that I can't apply the first purchase of Changing Phases Transformation to my second Hybrid Body Transformation; I have to modify the first Hybrid shape in order to modify the second, or I have to repurchase the same HBT after altering the first if I want to keep the same HBT without Attribute rating modification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:57:40-08:00","id":1288278,"title":"","content":"I don't think it really distinguishes between forms once you have them. You just need to take it twice if you want to modify both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:31:48-08:00","id":1288292,"title":"","content":"And now I want a charm that lets you swap out an existing Moon in Well Emanation spirit for you when you lose your last HL, retroactively revealing that you had swapped places with your spirit double some time previously. Or something.<br /> <br /> You could call it the Sha'a Oka Special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:34:04-08:00","id":1288294,"title":"","content":"You can buy HBT more than once? Where does it say that?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh sorry, you meant via Shifting Beast Nature, ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:49:02-08:00","id":1288300,"title":"","content":"Right now, I'm thinking that the Lunar Charms make me want to play a Lunar far more than the Solar Charms make me want to play a Solar. Any differential in power level is quite secondary to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:07:36-08:00","id":1288315,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to get why there are so many Lunars still alive. Wyld Hunts that go into Territories claimed by Elder Lunars either leave quickly, screaming, or do not leave at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T17:36:44-08:00","id":1288449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1288315#post1288315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to get why there are so many Lunars still alive. Wyld Hunts that go into Territories claimed by Elder Lunars either leave quickly, screaming, or do not leave at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that sometimes they let a couple of people leave to let everyone know exactly what happened to the ones that weren't allowed to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:14:49-08:00","id":1288486,"title":"","content":"Untamed Soul Unity is both a bonkers charms for basically Infinite Familiars, and also the Solar Bond part just had me going &quot;Awww...&quot; so many times (you got your Solar Squeeze/Best Solar Buddy a Tyrant Lizard for *insert occasion here*, its the best gift ever!). Its just a really heart-warming charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:39:13-08:00","id":1288494,"title":"","content":"Speaking of gifts, how about Heart-Affirming Tribute for making discount, mortal-useable artifacts out of nothing more than your heartfelt gratitude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:42:23-08:00","id":1288495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <