e fiction for the character creation chapter. And we are so very close to getting those martial arts charms unlocked!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:20:24-08:00","id":1289114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Raksi continued, \u201cWell, darling, what do you think of tearing apart upstart kingdoms, and of cannibalism?\u201d \u201cI liked living in peace. I love philosophy and books, but can\u2019t stand to see petty tyrants oppress the weak.\u201d Weyna said as she chewed the corner of her mouth. \u201cAs for the rest... I can\u2019t say I\u2019ve ever done anything like that.\u201d<br /> Raksi smiled, pointed fangs clipping over her bottom lip. \u201cA first time for everything.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Oh, Wenya, Wenya, Wenya.....<br /> <br /> And 800 dollars until more MA! Ar-woo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:53:52-08:00","id":1289121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289114#post1289114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, Wenya, Wenya, Wenya.....<br /> <br /> And 800 dollars until more MA! Ar-woo!</div> </div> </div> </div>In the years that followed, Weyna often wondered how much simpler her life would have been had she just bugged the f* out right there and then...<br /> <br /> Edit: I wonder what Weyna\u2019s Spirit Shape is? Something red.... hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T06:08:43-08:00","id":1289161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289114#post1289114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And 800 dollars until more MA! Ar-woo!</div> </div> </div> </div>The only known stretch goal after that is \u201cbeefier art budget\u201d.<br /> <br /> Did the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter reveal stretch goals only as they came up, too?<br /> <br /> And how far have we come, relative to how far the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter got?<br /> <br /> Some of us were concerned that Many-Faced Strangers wouldn\u2019t get as much enthusiasm as Heirs of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Though the devs seem to have avoided that by allowing us to load Strangers with more Exalted Charms and Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T06:27:36-08:00","id":1289166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289161#post1289161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only known stretch goal after that is \u201cbeefier art budget\u201d.<br /> <br /> Did the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter reveal stretch goals only as they came up, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's how OPP handle stretch goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And how far have we come, relative to how far the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter got? </div> </div> </div>About $10k under.<br /> <br /> Looking at Kicktraq, the difference isn't fewer backers - Fangs outpaces WFHW on that score - but lower average pledge. Fangs's average is about $110, WFHW's was about $140.<br /> <br /> I think part of the difference is due to WFHW having The Realm available in its pledge rewards, and Fangs not having an equivalent. Also Fangs being subject to higher shipping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 02-18-2019, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:09:50-08:00","id":1289171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289166#post1289166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the difference is due to WFHW having The Realm available in its pledge rewards, and Fangs not having an equivalent. Also Fangs being subject to higher shipping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the Realm, but also Lookshy, the Forest Witches, the new Forest Witch hotness with the Wanaasan, and that new Realm/Lookshy goodness with that new, younger empire over at the Dreaming Sea.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Fang Vanguard is completely new to Exalted, and it has no hype built up for it like previous editions have done for the various Dragon-Blooded institutions. No one really cared about any of Second Edition's Lunar factions, and none of them survived to Third Edition. Even the Silver Pact is unpopular with some people.<br /> <br /> Lunar domains aren't a big draw, either, since the Nameless Lair was an unremarkable boss-dungeon or (towards the end of Second Edition) a edgy-mcedgelord embarrassment. Raksi's boss-dungeon wasn't much better. Any other &quot;domains&quot; were just mortal kingdoms that Second Edition clumsily handed over to Lunar elders.<br /> <br /> This kickstarter and Fangs at the Gate has to build up hype for Lunar schools and domains right out of the gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:14:52-08:00","id":1289173,"title":"","content":"And we got MA styles! And a shapeshifting preview!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2419964\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2419964</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Lunar whose Tell is a physical feature may take a mutation, such as Gills or Unusual Hide, to represent it. The Tell\u2019s innate concealment doesn\u2019t prevent onlookers from noticing her mutation, but they must still roll to connect the Lunar with other forms they\u2019ve observed with the same Tell. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ok, sure, I only ever saw one guy with with gills and I just now saw an antelope with gills, but that's like just a coincidence man.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:16:39-08:00","id":1289174,"title":"","content":"New stretch goals are chapter fiction for Many Faced Strangers and a Lunars digital wallpaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:17:50-08:00","id":1289176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289173#post1289173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we got MA styles! And a shapeshifting preview!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2419964\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2419964</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, sure, I only ever saw one guy with with gills and I just now saw an antelope with gills, but that's like just a coincidence man.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Really. Nothing but awesome mental images.<br /> <br /> ... but technically by the rules, the gills (being a mutation possessed intrinsically) should disappear when shifted leaving gill shaped markings on the neck of the antelope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:21:20-08:00","id":1289177,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She loses any mutations she possesses intrinsically (but not those granted by Charms), <b>with the exception of mutations tied to her Tell.&quot;</b></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:21:54-08:00","id":1289178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289177#post1289177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She loses any mutations she possesses intrinsically (but not those granted by Charms), <b>with the exception of mutations tied to her Tell.&quot;</b></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, missed that part. Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:22:46-08:00","id":1289179,"title":"","content":"Actually, on that note, I suppose you could throw in subtlety to have a functional tell that works like a regular one for the purposes of being spotted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:31:46-08:00","id":1289181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289171#post1289171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just the Realm, but also Lookshy, the Forest Witches, the new Forest Witch hotness with the Wanaasan, and that new Realm/Lookshy goodness with that new, younger empire over at the Dreaming Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was WFHW had the Realm book included in its available pledge rewards. Fangs doesn't have an equivalent. (Many-Faced Strangers is the Lunar version of Heirs to the Shogunate, but there's nothing matching the Realm book.)<br /> <br /> Basically, I honestly don't think the issue is disinterest in Many-Faced Strangers. My suspicion is that the issue is a financial one more than anything else. Remember, Fangs currently has <i>more</i> backers than WFHW did at this point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:31:54-08:00","id":1289182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289174#post1289174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New stretch goals are chapter fiction for Many Faced Strangers and a Lunars digital wallpaper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be pleasantly surprised if we reached that far.<br /> <br /> We've already got additional elders, additional animals, and additional Martial Arts. While there still could be plenty of potential backers who simply haven't bought in yet, I don't see anything that would really motivate most people who have already backed the project to contribute a little more.<br /> <br /> Now, if one of those goals was &quot;additional sorcery initiations or spells&quot; or &quot;additional artifacts&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:34:05-08:00","id":1289184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289179#post1289179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, on that note, I suppose you could throw in subtlety to have a functional tell that works like a regular one for the purposes of being spotted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're willing to spend the Merit points or Bonus Points at chargen for that additional mutation, yeah. Or maybe you can mutate yourself afterwards with an Intelligence Charm or sorcerous working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:48:38-08:00","id":1289187,"title":"","content":"Or just take Moon\u2019s Hidden Face","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:52:50-08:00","id":1289190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289182#post1289182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be pleasantly surprised if we reached that far.<br /> <br /> We've already got additional elders, additional animals, and additional Martial Arts. While there still could be plenty of potential backers who simply haven't bought in yet, I don't see anything that would really motivate most people who have already backed the project to contribute a little more.<br /> <br /> Now, if one of those goals was &quot;additional sorcery initiations or spells&quot; or &quot;additional artifacts&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>wouldn't</i> be surprised; average daily pledge would have to drop spectacularly (like, below $500 a day for the next three weeks, to give us under $10k total, and then under $10k total again for the final stretch) not to make both of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:31:46-08:00","id":1289207,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifting preview leads to some questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When she takes an action the animal has a listed dice pool for, she may use its dice pool. Any dice over her own base (Attribute + Ability) pool count as Charm dice and are subject to her dice cap (p. XX), potentially preventing her from using a form\u2019s full dice pool. </div> </div> </div>So the primary advantage of taking a form with, say, a better Stealth pool than yours would be to save motes on Excellency use (or to get around not having the relevant Excellency), as you would not be able to exceed your own native Dex + Stealth + (Dexcellency) value? If you're bad at something, or have a low Attribute, taking the form of an animal which excels at it won't be as useful.<br /> <br /> (A character would need Strength 5 + Brawl 4 to be able to use all of a giant constrictor's 14 control roll dice in a grapple, right? - never turn into a giant snake, it never helps.)<br /> <br /> It's tidy to keep the dice pool range within the normal limits. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She may use the animal\u2019s natural weapons, including their listed dice pool and damage value. (Note that she uses the same pool for <b>withering </b>and <b>decisive </b>attacks). Any dice over her own base (Dexterity + Brawl) count as Charm dice, but damage doesn\u2019t count against the amount she may add with the Strength Excellency. </div> </div> </div>So you'll need Dex 5, Brawl 3 (or Dex 4/Brawl 5) to benefit from all of a great cat's 13-die claw attack dice pool, yeah? (And couldn't benefit from its +3 dice from Ambush hunter unless your cap was 3 higher - does the stunting in a second Attribute apply here?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:37:59-08:00","id":1289208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289207#post1289207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the primary advantage of taking a form with, say, a better Stealth pool than yours would be to save motes on Excellency use</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I think so. Though some forms have useful merits.<br /> My PC's totem is a viper. My own stealth pool is actually better anyway, but if I'm sliding through grass or jungle, I get double 9s from the Camouflage merit. Plus of course, a human can't hide in regular grass while a small viper can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you'll need Dex 5, Brawl 3 (or Dex 4/Brawl 5) to benefit from all of a great cat's 13-die claw attack dice pool, yeah? (And couldn't benefit from its +3 dice from Ambush hunter unless your cap was 3 higher </div> </div> </div>I believe so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - does the stunting in a second Attribute apply here?) </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> One key thing I noticed, is that because you don't get Accuracy bonuses, actually it's generally better to use the animal's &quot;heavy weapons&quot;... unless you're trying to save motes, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:16:03-08:00","id":1289487,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2420988\" target=\"_blank\">Character Creation and Traits preview.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:30:33-08:00","id":1289491,"title":"","content":"Okay wow, those merits are awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:23:07-08:00","id":1289515,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a hell a lot of of mutations. The caste powers are cool too.<br /> <br /> I love Ocean Pearl's rather aggrieved tone in their quote: \u201cNo one living knows the demon\u2019s secret name, they say? How rude; they seem to have forgotten about me.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T08:30:40-08:00","id":1289536,"title":"","content":"The new Merits are great, and it's going to be harder to pick which ones to grab.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Full Moon anima, always the best in previous Editions, returns in its adapted glory, and with two awesome new tricks!<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon anima is exactly what I asked for! Something that helps them succeed in their Caste role as the Full Moon's anima powers help them, while leaving &quot;disguise and face-wearing&quot; to universal Lunar capabilities in Charms and social Attributes.<br /> <br /> The No Moon anima is... Well, it's definitely far superior to previous Editions, for sure, but I'm not immediately sold or excited by the &quot;sense and identify places of power&quot; trick, and the shadow veil thing doesn't seem as exciting next to the Full Moon and Changing Moon tricks, but it's certainly useful for thwarting attacks and Read Intention actions, though it would be self-defeating to try and use it to assist with Stealth actions. Then again, their third power is pretty beastly at most if not all of the things a No Moon became a No Moon to do.<br /> <br /> The Casteless anima power is new and hot. I can definitely see some people being tempted to remain Casteless for this, at least until they can get the universal Charm for assisting with rapid shapeshifting. Even if you have your heart set on a specific Caste, you can feel powerful and versatile until you get one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Love the role bonuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm still ruling that Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style is an exception to the restriction of Martial Arts in animal forms. You're attacking with your voice, not your body, and that's something whales can already do, and that songbirds and roaring lions ought to be able to do as easily as humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> I LOVE the new Lunar Limit Breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-19-2019, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T08:56:02-08:00","id":1289544,"title":"","content":"Lunars spending more BP on attributes at base than Solars, Dragonblooded, or Mortals is a terrible decision, borne out if a misguided attempt to give casteless lunars some bonus with BP. This is stupid.<br /> <br /> Not only do Lunars already suffer in BP from the combination of being unable to favor abilities and being unable to raise abilities above 3 without BP, but they also apparently buy attributes besides their core ones at an increased cost, creating even more of a game of system mastery where it is incentivized to raise your non favored attributes with free dots, and your favored ones only with bp and xp.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is leaving aside how expensive BP chargen is for lunars: a single ability at 5 costs double the price as a solar, deeb or mortal getting one to 5, while the cost reduction for attributes that lunars should be seeing works out to a single extra dot per chargen, at most, and only if every dot they buy is favored/caste costed.<br /> <br /> An average solar will leave chargen with 3 attributes at 5, and a smattering of 3-1s, and have 5 abilities at 5.<br /> <br /> An average lunar will leave chargen with 4 attributes at 5, and a smattering of 3-1s, and have 0 abilities above 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To truly balance this out would make attributes too cheap for many (50% discount as favored abilities are, so 2bp per attribute). But the developers should at least not create problems with the chargen, specifically so they can have casteless gain a tiny stupid benefit. 3bp for caste and favored, 4bp otherwise is still overcosted, but is at least *equivalent* to solars/deebs/mortals, who pay 4 dots for their primary and secondary attributes, and 3 for their tertiary. Instead of worse than them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 02-19-2019, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:13:43-08:00","id":1289553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289544#post1289544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is leaving aside how expensive BP chargen is for lunars: a single ability at 5 costs double the price as a solar, deeb or mortal getting one to 5, while the cost reduction for attributes that lunars should be seeing works out to a single extra dot per chargen, at most, and only if every dot they buy is favored/caste costed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals don't get favoured abilities in 3e. They would pay just as much to raise one to 5 as a lunar would.<br /> <br /> Also are you factoring the extra 3 dots of attributes lunars automatically get into those averages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:24:31-08:00","id":1289557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289544#post1289544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars spending more BP on attributes at base than Solars, Dragonblooded, or Mortals is a terrible decision, borne out if a misguided attempt to give casteless lunars some bonus with BP. This is stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a practical point of view a player could choose to put fewer of their initial points in their caste and favored attributes leaving more points for the non favored, they could then use their freebies to increase their favored and caste attributes at three freebies per point, a value that other character types only get for their tertiary abilities. The lunar also get an additional dot in each of their three areas.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the best attribute spread and the lowest freebie cost to raise their attributes. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:24:51-08:00","id":1289558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289553#post1289553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Also are you factoring the extra 3 dots of attributes lunars automatically get into those averages?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am. If you want to completely min-max it, a lunar can currently start with 6 attributes at 5, but the other 3 will be at 1. This is actually 'technically' optimal from a chargen perspective, if you wanted to max all 9: make sure 3 of your favored/caste ones are at 1, then max those with xp.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Apromoor^<br /> <br /> I addressed that in the post. The split between 3/5 cost wise increases the push to raise non favored attributes with your free dots, and use bp to actually be good at what your favored/caste says you should be. I think this is bad design, that creates 'game of chargen' imbalances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 02-19-2019, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:28:10-08:00","id":1289559,"title":"","content":"I mean that is literally how you minmax abilities for ability exalts so honestly I'm ok with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:09:47-08:00","id":1289574,"title":"","content":"Solar character gen is way too min-maxable if you know what you're doing. Someone on this forum described it as &quot;a winnable mini-game.&quot; Which is terrible.<br /> <br /> But Lunar character gen? Yeah, it's pretty fine. You can min-max it a bit if you know what you're doing, but not so much, and not in ways that won't cause you serious short-term issues.<br /> <br /> So, basically, I don't think comparing it to Solar character gen is a good idea. That's just comparing a well-designed system to a badly-designed system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kittyempress</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The split between 3/5 cost wise increases the push to raise non favored attributes with your free dots, and use bp to actually be good at what your favored/caste says you should be. I think this is bad design, that creates 'game of chargen' imbalances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's the opposite, because it's more like the XP cost.<br /> <br /> For Solars, the freebie cost encourages you to go big on a few Abilities (up to 7 abilities at 5).<br /> The XP cost, on the other hand, encourages you to spend it broadening out your abilities, as it's dirt-cheap to raise low abilities to medium.<br /> <br /> Combined, this heavily encourages min-maxing. The system tells you to start with a min-maxed character, because it'll be easy to fill your holes in play. Whereas starting with a broad character and then specialising is way harder.<br /> <br /> That's why Solar character gen is a winnable mini-game (and it's even worse if you're making a character who starts with XP, for example if your character dies and you make a new character to join an Essence 3 group).<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, Lunar character gen encourages you to put your points into favoured attributes, and the XP system encourages you to put your points into favoured or low attributes.<br /> <br /> Now, that might still encourage you to min-max, but because of the way you have to place Attributes into the three categories, you're not likely to have many Attributes at 1, the way a Solar will have lots of Abilities at 0 or 1.<br /> You can't, say, go big on Physical and completely dump Mental because you have to put at least 5 dots in Mental attributes anyway.<br /> There's also the fact that, unlike Solars, your Attributes are not divisible by 4. You literally can't have Perception 5, Intelligence 1, Wits 5 with your starting dots the way a Solar can.<br /> <br /> It's not perfect of course. But I think it's good enough to not be a big issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:24:44-08:00","id":1289579,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's see what the most min-maxed Lunar I can come up with is at character gen.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Charisma 5, Manipulation 1, Appearance 2<br /> <br /> Perception 4, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> <br /> Now I have 15 freebies. I'm not spending anything on Abilities or Charms, obviously.<br /> <br /> So already, my highest pool is only 8.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right, I'm a Full Moon, so I have two physical Caste attributes. I'll go Dexterity and Stamina. 9 freebies spent on Stamina puts it to 5 (that's worth 27xp... hmm, only a 3-1 return. Not great, but I can't see a better one for now).<br /> Then I have to put a Favoured attribute in Mental. We'll put it in Perception, and buy a 5th dot for 3 freebies (woo, 4-1 return).<br /> <br /> I've got 3 freebies left. Appearance 3? That's rubbish, 2-1 return.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll buy a 4th dot of my combat Ability (3-1 return) and like another Specialty or something.<br /> <br /> So now I have:</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> Charisma 5, Manipulation 1, Appearance 2<br /> Perception 5, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> 1x Ability at 4 (+1)<br /> 3x Abilities at 3 (+1)<br /> 5x Abilities at 3<br /> 1x Ability at 1<br /> 15x Abilities at 0<br /> <br /> Yeah... it's min-maxed. But I don't even have a single pool at 11.<br /> <br /> Whereas the min-maxed Solar:<br /> Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 1<br /> Charisma 5, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1<br /> Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> 4x Abilities at 5 (+1)<br /> 3x Abilities at 5<br /> 1x Ability at 4<br /> 1x Ability at 3<br /> 1x Ability at 1<br /> 15x Ability at 0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:42:40-08:00","id":1289584,"title":"","content":"Anyway.<br /> <br /> Merits seem comprehensive. There's something for most totems.<br /> <br /> The anima powers...<br /> <br /> Full Moons' powers aren't conceptually exciting, but are mechanically strong. A bit like Dawns.<br /> Changing Moons'... to my surprise have powers that also are not conceptually exciting (compared to say, the Eclipse), but are also mechanically strong.<br /> <br /> No Moons' powers could be argued to be the weakest.<br /> The first is somewhat wide-ranging, but pricey for what it does (though it is cap-breaking).<br /> The once/day power is strong for sorcerers or those who do big stuff in downtime and don't mind flaring. Say, a crafter deep underground. But... not that useful for others. Still, the previous two do cover a very large portion of No Moon characters. And weirdly, you can use it as a stealth power. Which, combined with the first power, shows No Moons as actually a very sneaky lot, despite neither being the Dexterity-Caste or the Tricksters. I kind of like that.<br /> <br /> But the most interesting power to me is the one where you say &quot;ST, please lead me to a place of adventure and power! Did I mention I get 5 non-charm auto-successes to find it?&quot;<br /> My ST is actually really good at making up weird ancient ruins, so this intrigues me, though my No Moon is currently training with the Pact while I play a Zenith. It does encourage me to bring him back in future though.<br /> <br /> Casteless as the most shapeshifter-y? I have to say, I didn't expect it, but I like it. Fitting and useful.<br /> Sadly, the two Casteless currently being played are not, actually, big into shapeshifting, unlike my old Casteless. But getting to choose the once/day power is useful for them, as they're both kind of all-rounders.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Casteless, having only 2 Favoured attributes compared to the Castes' 2 Favoured+2 Caste, but getting charms from the other 7 attributes at 9xp each, is not at all what I expected.<br /> But... I think it kind of works. Certainly, I intend to buy charms from all over for my character Dr Soma. And I can always specialise after I get tattoos.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:53:29-08:00","id":1289586,"title":"","content":"Huh... I can't see anywhere how much Universal Charms cost. Are they Unfavoured? Favoured? I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> RAW, I guess they're Unfavoured, but that seems somehow surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:04:04-08:00","id":1289589,"title":"","content":"Favoured. <br /> <br /> I don't know where it says, but that's WoG about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:31:06-08:00","id":1289629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289544#post1289544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels a little early for doomsaying, and could definitely be articulated more politely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289544#post1289544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is leaving aside how expensive BP chargen is for lunars: a single ability at 5 costs double the price as a solar, deeb or mortal getting one to 5...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is this untrue (as others have pointed out, mortals don't have Favored Abilities), but it's only true for Solars and Dragon-Blooded who are raising a <i>Favored</i> Ability to 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289544#post1289544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An average lunar will leave chargen with 4 attributes at 5, and a smattering of 3-1s, and have 0 abilities above 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again this feels a bit premature. Especially since a Lunar who focuses on a particular niche like sorcery will likely still want to max out his dice pool.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:49:00-08:00","id":1289637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289589#post1289589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Favoured.<br /> <br /> I don't know where it says, but that's WoG about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked Vance anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since a Lunar who focuses on a particular niche like sorcery will likely still want to max out his dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly.<br /> It does cost 4bp to get an Ability at 5, but that's not extremely expensive.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's only a couple of dice different; it's not like Solars, who need the high abilities for their excellencies as well, and of course to get the charms.<br /> <br /> With a 2-dice stunt channelling the right attributes, a Lunar could roll 23 dice for sorcery.<br /> If they didn't bother buying their Occult to 5... they could roll 21 dice.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's something you can do, and might well want to, but it's not an auto-pick. You might want to spend those 4bp on something else.<br /> <br /> Which... is good design, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:02:43-08:00","id":1289647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289637#post1289637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked Vance anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Possibly.<br /> It does cost 4bp to get an Ability at 5, but that's not extremely expensive.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's only a couple of dice different; it's not like Solars, who need the high abilities for their excellencies as well, and of course to get the charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that lunars have is better broad applicability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:55:13-08:00","id":1289700,"title":"","content":"I'm not totally sold on the No-Moon anima powers. But then I was iffy on the Twilight Anima powers too. &quot;Ooh, I can locate/teleport to a nearby weird place&quot; doesn't really seem particularly useful or relevant to me, nor entirely fitting for the castes in question. I'm also a little unclear on what the Shadowy Penumbra applies to. Does it include attacks against you?<br /> <br /> I do like the ability to Nom their anima and get a free full mental excellency/willpower/sorcerous motes though.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also would enjoy a short sidebar or something in the Solar Bond section that basically says &quot;Solars do not, by default, automatically get a Tie to their Lunar upon first meeting them but they can if they want to.&quot; I want my Jalith x Nala meetings darn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:45:06-08:00","id":1289718,"title":"","content":"One other thing re: attribute costs. I think trying to max out attributes is the wrong way to go about it. We know they're getting charms to substitute attributes for one another. They're not <i>designed</i> to have a shitload of attributes at max. They're designed to <i>not need them.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:29:44-08:00","id":1289735,"title":"","content":"Heck I'm just happy that Casteless now are <i>good </i>at shapeshifting as opposed to Second Edition where they were actually penalized for shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:38:38-08:00","id":1289736,"title":"","content":"They were both good at it <i>and</i> penalised for doing it, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:22:54-08:00","id":1289755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289718#post1289718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing re: attribute costs. I think trying to max out attributes is the wrong way to go about it. We know they're getting charms to substitute attributes for one another. They're not <i>designed</i> to have a shitload of attributes at max. They're designed to <i>not need them.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Even if this is true, I still find it kinda off-putting from a game perspective. The attribute exalt are the ones with the highest attribute cost, which goes away after chargen for some reason.<br /> <br /> I'd rather there just be no favored BP cost if it's game breaking, I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:38:18-08:00","id":1289762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289718#post1289718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing re: attribute costs. I think trying to max out attributes is the wrong way to go about it. We know they're getting charms to substitute attributes for one another. They're not <i>designed</i> to have a shitload of attributes at max. They're designed to <i>not need them.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I want to preface my statement by saying I basically agree with what Elfive is saying.<br /> <br /> As a soon to be Lunar player, I think/wonder if the way forward would be as so:<br /> <br /> 1. Max out your Caste Attribute with the basic dots/BP<br /> <br /> 2. Have a maxed favoured Attribute in both of the other two Attribute groupings that aren\u2019t your caste favoured.<br /> <br /> 3. Have about 2 or 3 in all other attributes.<br /> <br /> 4. Always be stunting your +5 Attributes in your rolls if needed<br /> <br /> So 4 Attributes at 5, the rest at 3. Doable...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T22:16:34-08:00","id":1289811,"title":"","content":"So yeah, with some back of the napkin calculation with no chicanery about mixing Favored Attributes vs Caste Attributes this is what I got (Full Moon):<br /> <br /> Str 5<br /> Dex 2<br /> Sta 5<br /> <br /> Cha 5<br /> Man 3<br /> App 3<br /> <br /> Int 2<br /> Per 2<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> With a 6bp surcharge. If you are okay with 2s then you can spend the bps elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Seems reasonably solid for minimal math to me? Maybe max one important Ability to 5, for 4bp keep everything else at 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-20-2019, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T22:37:11-08:00","id":1289816,"title":"","content":"Starting the character creation process (won't finish till we have the full charmset of course), I'm playing around with my Snakewoman Lunar with a Mongoose Spirit Shape. These are the mutations I've landed on starting with - <br /> <br /> For her &quot;human&quot; true form: Fangs (3), Venomous (4), Serpentine (4), Snaketongue (1)<br /> <br /> Hybrid Body Transformation: Extra Limbs (3), Ambidexterous (2), Unusual Hide (1) - she gains a fur coat and sprouts two hind legs; she's able to use all four limbs supported by her tail, or use her legs for support while weaponizing her tail<br /> <br /> Perfect Hybrid Interaction adds Hypermobility (4)<br /> <br /> <br /> At Essence 2, her next Perfect Hybrid Interaction purchase will throw Constrictor (3) in the mix and boost Unusual Hide by one; then maybe Silent Movement (3) and Vibration Sense (1) at Essence 3; throw in Wall Climbing (4) at Essence 4.... you get the idea. She's the nightmare that darts in the shadows to a culture of Snakefolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:37:25-08:00","id":1289832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289816#post1289816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting the character creation process (won't finish till we have the full charmset of course), I'm playing around with my Snakewoman Lunar with a Mongoose Spirit Shape. These are the mutations I've landed on starting with - <br /> <br /> For her &quot;human&quot; true form: Fangs (3), Venomous (4), Serpentine (4), Snaketongue (1)<br /> <br /> Hybrid Body Transformation: Extra Limbs (3), Ambidexterous (2), Unusual Hide (1) - she gains a fur coat and sprouts two hind legs; she's able to use all four limbs supported by her tail, or use her legs for support while weaponizing her tail<br /> <br /> Perfect Hybrid Interaction adds Hypermobility (4)<br /> <br /> <br /> At Essence 2, her next Perfect Hybrid Interaction purchase will throw Constrictor (3) in the mix and boost Unusual Hide by one; then maybe Silent Movement (3) and Vibration Sense (1) at Essence 3; throw in Wall Climbing (4) at Essence 4.... you get the idea. She's the nightmare that darts in the shadows to a culture of Snakefolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m probably missing something here. You have 12 points of Mutations in your base human form, mutations that presumably have to be paid out of your bp dots. <br /> <br /> So is that where you want to spend the bulk of 15bps?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, forgot Merit dots continue on then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-20-2019, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T01:37:28-08:00","id":1289846,"title":"","content":"PHI is an essence 2 charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:14:42-08:00","id":1290022,"title":"","content":"Just make non favored cost 4bp as anyone else. <br /> Solar and Deeb still have ter so they also pay 3 bp for their worst attribute which is 3 out of 9, while Lunars have 4/9 <br /> It just looks stupid imo, making castless viable is something they did very good through in game with less pay for raising unfavored and buying charms so chargen doesn't need to be different with the attribute cost of bp if that is one of the main arguments <br /> The system just keep promoting the bad bp/xp split","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:08:07-08:00","id":1290049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1289846#post1289846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PHI is an essence 2 charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boo, missed that. I guess Hypermobility will have to wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:01:40-08:00","id":1290747,"title":"","content":"...Many-Armed Warrior Panoply is the Sublime Danger charm, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Have we seen Quicksilver Second Face yet? I'm not seeing it.<br /> <br /> Lunars do Monster Hunter style Crafting really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-22-2019, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:13:13-08:00","id":1290752,"title":"","content":"Think it's interesting to have Unerring Fang Technique and Striking Mospid Method as charms in the same set that can be combined together.<br /> Is this a response to Solar builds that are scared to lose any initiative/overly depend on stealing it from missed attacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:03:27-08:00","id":1290759,"title":"","content":"I notice Dex has a lot of &quot;if you have more init than opponent&quot; triggers in its charms. Also a bunch of disarming charms, which kind of makes sense. A Lunar without a weapon is much more dangerous than anyone else without a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:05:49-08:00","id":1290761,"title":"","content":"Foe Baiting Sidestep: *Meep, Meep*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:11:07-08:00","id":1290773,"title":"","content":"Some of these charms are straight up better then their solar variants, which is pretty curious. <br /> <br /> Specifically looking at Gleaming Crescent Block and Sensing the Deadly Flow here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:32:37-08:00","id":1290780,"title":"","content":"Shadow-Chased Silver Defense feels like a joke reference back to 1e, where charms could allow you to both parry and dodge an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:58:36-08:00","id":1290789,"title":"","content":"Bombardier Spittle Alchemy gives me the happys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:13:02-08:00","id":1290792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1290773#post1290773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of these charms are straight up better then their solar variants, which is pretty curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to remember that the &quot;power levels&quot; of various types of Exalts are, in 3e, being considered <i>holistically</i>, rather than charm-by-charm. That means that looking at a single charm and comparing it to the equivalent in another charmset isn't really a useful metric any more. What matters is whether the whole charmset, when considered together, is more powerful. Which means Lunars can legitimately have charms that are more powerful than Solar equivalents, as long as, for instance, a Solar specialized in Melee or Brawl has a pretty good chance of beating a Lunar similarly specialized into Dex or Str. While we obviously haven't seen all of the Lunar charms yet, I think that's still the way things are heading. An equal-Essence Lunar with similar investment in combat charms will give a Melee-Supernal Solar a good fight, but I'm still going to bet on the Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:22:50-08:00","id":1290796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1290759#post1290759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice Dex has a lot of &quot;if you have more init than opponent&quot; triggers in its charms. Also a bunch of disarming charms, which kind of makes sense. A Lunar without a weapon is much more dangerous than anyone else without a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, conversely it looks like a Dexterity favoured Lunar might be in for a really bad time if they get crashed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:30:34-08:00","id":1290800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1290792#post1290792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's important to remember that the &amp;quot;power levels&amp;quot; of various types of Exalts are, in 3e, being considered <i>holistically</i>, rather than charm-by-charm. That means that looking at a single charm and comparing it to the equivalent in another charmset isn't really a useful metric any more. What matters is whether the whole charmset, when considered together, is more powerful. Which means Lunars can legitimately have charms that are more powerful than Solar equivalents, as long as, for instance, a Solar specialized in Melee or Brawl has a pretty good chance of beating a Lunar similarly specialized into Dex or Str. While we obviously haven't seen all of the Lunar charms yet, I think that's still the way things are heading. An equal-Essence Lunar with similar investment in combat charms will give a Melee-Supernal Solar a good fight, but I'm still going to bet on the Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be the case but seeing charms that are out and out the same effect, just a few motes cheaper, is still very surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:56:12-08:00","id":1290860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1290049#post1290049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Boo, missed that. I guess Hypermobility will have to wait!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m am pleased to say that a lot of what I wanted to do with mutations I ran out of points for are achievable without Dex Charms!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:52:18-08:00","id":1290945,"title":"","content":"Dexterity lunars really love disarm gambits, best way for a sidereal to beat a lunar is unarmed kung fu prowess confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:15:21-08:00","id":1291037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1285063#post1285063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is purely a feature of our Aeon Exalted setting hack, and entirely in absence of any manuscript. <br /> <br /> But! <br /> <br /> Our Lunars will have a Lair, inspired by but not directly lifted from Beast. The Lair can connect to any place where the Lunar has a territory, including places in other Aeons. (Aeons being a pocket realm, such as the dead corpus of a long ago nation or religion.) The Lair is attached directly as a feature of the Exaltation, and there are some story elements for Lunars going on experimenting with and building through them. Inside the Lair, all the Lunar's shapes are present, as is their panoply. So, they have a hideout, a thematically intrinsic way to travel around, and built-in storage equivalent to Elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Whether this will require some Charms or be completely intrinsic from the start is yet to be determined - in our Chronicle we're still doing the initial set of reveals about the existence of Aeons (*) and dropping a few clues about how they work. By the time we have the Lunars manuscripts in our eager paws, my players will know pretty well what they're dealing with. In the meantime, the NPC Lunars have an unexplained talent for vanishing entirely out of Creation and popping up somewhere else in a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> Presented purely to share the idea!<br /> <br /> <br /> (*) Coming Saturday's session will have us going to our first semi-stable Aeon. I'm looking forward to sending the Solars into the dead husk of the Empire of Xaarr. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty solid idea! Really dig the Aeon stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:30:26-08:00","id":1291041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcod