rd-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T05:54:17-08:00","id":1293451,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">What do you guys think of the artefacts? If you'd had a chance to read them.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The first two I found a bit similar, and the stinging blades were just okay.<br /> The chain that used to be a serpent I thought was okay; the charms weren't didn't grab me on first glance, but it would have a lot of stunt fodder with swinging about and stuff. And it has a cool back-story.<br /> I quite liked the bow that cures people and turns fae into animals though.<br /> The pipes were nice for a Lunar bard, which is not a concept I'd play but others might. Something nice and sweet and pleasant.<br /> The mirror was kind of cool but would give your character serious issues. You'd need to mix it with some confidence-building activities.<br /> The warpstone gun also, well, makes you insane, but honestly the warpstone gun is hilarious fun. Spraying mutations and madness all over the place, I'd definitely take that.<br /> Death at the Root could be good, but destroying manses is maybe a bit marginal for most PCs. I think it depends on your game, and how much it features Manses and Demesnes.<br /> I also liked the spiky berzerker armour, though it's a pity it's silver and not black. Maybe you could paint it black and get some nice fur and a back-banner.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"li