Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T14:47:16-08:00","id":1293892,"title":"","content":"Lunar's court might be nice, to give Lunar Luna-Worship a bit more weight.<br /> <br /> I liked both of the Dominions out today; Sunken Luthe as a cosmopolitan centre of art was not at all expected, but I loved that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T14:50:34-08:00","id":1293894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1293887#post1293887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Luna's court? That's neat.<br /> <br /> They said that Sublime Danger and her Thousand-Daiklaves Style might be a stretch goal, but apparently one beyond even &amp;quot;lunar deities&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>James confirmed in Kickstarter comments that she\u2019s about three unrevealed stretchgoals (not just unreached stretchgoals) away from where we are now (technically he said four, but that was before the Sorcery stretchgoal was revealed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T14:53:53-08:00","id":1293896,"title":"","content":"So, no mention of treating the descendants of the dragon blooded like shit in Luthe so far. Looks like Leviathan might be working through his grief in a slightly more healthy manner this time around (but only slightly since they still spent a millennia or so not doing much because they were super depressed). Or they just didn't get to that part in the preview, guess we will find out tomorrow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T16:17:46-08:00","id":1293915,"title":"","content":"Haven\u2019t digested all of the preview, are what is the Lunar Equivalent to Supernal Abilities, for Dragonblooded it was Signature element charms. What is it for Lunars, the Totem Keyword, or the generalized nature of Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T16:27:23-08:00","id":1293916,"title":"","content":"They seem to have two, totem abilities that allow them to learn certain charms with an alternate attribute and the protean keyword that gives them a bonus effect to some charms if they are shape shifted into certain forms when using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T16:32:32-08:00","id":1293918,"title":"","content":"The equivalent to Solar Supernal has been stated IIRC to be Shapeshifting, into various animal or human forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T05:56:12-08:00","id":1294014,"title":"","content":"And now, <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2432121\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Dominions</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T12:32:12-08:00","id":1294131,"title":"","content":"Apparently, Raksi executes the people whose punishments are beyond what even she does.<br /> <br /> Given how what would make Raksi a little queasy would cause most of Creation to seriously consider carving out their own eyes, that seems fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T12:55:42-08:00","id":1294142,"title":"","content":"So not only does he no longer treat the descendants of the dragon blooded like shit, Leviathan actively protects dragon blooded in his service from people that do want to be shit heads like that. They have really made him a way cooler dude this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T13:10:37-08:00","id":1294147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294142#post1294142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not only does he no longer treat the descendants of the dragon blooded like shit, Leviathan actively protects dragon blooded in his service from people that do want to be shit heads like that. They have really made him a way cooler dude this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the sense he doesn't like them, but knows that's his grief and self-loathing talking, and he tries to overcome it. Which yeah, makes him Coolest Orca.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T14:10:41-08:00","id":1294171,"title":"","content":"Just a little under a thousand dollars more to go until we get another Caul expansion and write up for Sha\u2019a Oka","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:11:53-08:00","id":1294262,"title":"","content":"The Lunar Dominions are all so good! I think my favorite is still the Mountain of the Spider King, but the Nameless Lair, Mahalanka and Luthe are all so different now, and all such interesting and developed locations, it's really worthwhile. There's a great slice of examples running everything from Lunars as reigning livings gods, ancient divine founders, equal partners and allies to their patronized cultures, and fearsome trickster figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:17:05-08:00","id":1294269,"title":"","content":"Dominions definitely feel weaker than the previous parts of the manuscript but not bad by any means just kind of bland.<br /> <br /> I am still of two minds when it comes to the Caul. From the dragonblooded POV we have a great adventure path shaping up. Travel to each city and fight their themed boss in a interesting locale and then continue.<br /> <br /> From a Lunar POV though it feels much more lacklustre. You can't really interact with any of the lions generals because they are basically just card board cut outs waiting to be beheaded by a sworn kinship. You can't even really interact with the black lion since from the writing so far he seems to be half crazy and nobody no where he is most of the time.<br /> <br /> I am still baffled by why someone would want to play a lunar game on the caul since it feels like your only options are being ignored by a bunch of second rate dark souls bosses or help lion man skeletor fail to take castle Greyskull once a week.<br /> <br /> To be really clear I am looking forward to the dragon blooded caul Adventure path I am just a little sad it is eating up lunar word count, I would of preferred if the kickstarter had a stronger focus on giving lunars interesting options as players not just as props for other exalt games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:30:16-08:00","id":1294276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294269#post1294269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominions definitely feel weaker than the previous parts of the manuscript but not bad by any means just kind of bland.<br /> <br /> I am still of two minds when it comes to the Caul. From the dragonblooded POV we have a great adventure path shaping up. Travel to each city and fight their themed boss in a interesting locale and then continue.<br /> <br /> From a Lunar POV though it feels much more lacklustre. You can't really interact with any of the lions generals because they are basically just card board cut outs waiting to be beheaded by a sworn kinship. You can't even really interact with the black lion since from the writing so far he seems to be half crazy and nobody no where he is most of the time.<br /> <br /> I am still baffled by why someone would want to play a lunar game on the caul since it feels like your only options are being ignored by a bunch of second rate dark souls bosses or help lion man skeletor fail to take castle Greyskull once a week.<br /> <br /> To be really clear I am looking forward to the dragon blooded caul Adventure path I am just a little sad it is eating up lunar word count, I would of preferred if the kickstarter had a stronger focus on giving lunars interesting options as players not just as props for other exalt games.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it\u2019s not a good setting for Lunars because they\u2019re winning? Your assumption of \u201cfailing to take Castle Greyskull\u201d, precludes the most obvious Lunar Adventure path: push out the colonists once and for all and take Faxai as your own seat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:43:11-08:00","id":1294284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294269#post1294269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominions definitely feel weaker than the previous parts of the manuscript but not bad by any means just kind of bland.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. For the the Dominions chapter is really great. They are full of fantastic locations and also showcase varying ways that a Lunar might interact with their dominion from god king/queen to mystic founder to haunting devil. I will however agree that the Caul was the weakest example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 03-05-2019, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T20:10:05-08:00","id":1294295,"title":"","content":"235K hit so stretch goal reached.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T20:10:22-08:00","id":1294296,"title":"","content":"I have reached the words &quot;tame great flying eels&quot; and now my life is complete. <br /> <br /> And Aum-Ashatra is a surprisingly cool dude, I guess. He's no <i>great flying eel</i> though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T20:42:56-08:00","id":1294305,"title":"","content":"Now we need to make flying eels face flying sharks in a death match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:04:13-08:00","id":1294311,"title":"","content":"Am I the only person who saw italicized descriptors of Territories and thought &quot;Ooo, that suggests new mechanics to come.&quot;?<br /> Maybe lunar specific, or maybe not generalized mechanics for ruling a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:44:56-08:00","id":1294321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294311#post1294311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only person who saw italicized descriptors of Territories and thought &quot;Ooo, that suggests new mechanics to come.&quot;?<br /> Maybe lunar specific, or maybe not generalized mechanics for ruling a place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about mechanics to come, but they do refer to mechanics in the Lunars book - the territory-claiming charm Boundary-Marking Meditation lets a Lunar declare up to three traits their territory has, which acts as a bonus to actions that fit with them, or a penalty when acting against them, to anyone in the territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T22:27:17-08:00","id":1294328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294269#post1294269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominions definitely feel weaker than the previous parts of the manuscript but not bad by any means just kind of bland.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's the best chapter (fluff-wise; you can't really compare it to charms).<br /> The history and Silver Pact chapters were decent, nothing to complain about, but didn't grab me. While I liked some of the artefacts, I didn't find their stories riveting.<br /> But about two-thirds of the Dominions made me want to run a game involving them. I really like most of them, and the ones I don't love are still good. <br /> <br /> I also like how a)being so far into the threshold, they flesh out more areas of the setting, like the North-East and the Cinder Coast, b)they show a variety of examples of how Lunars can interact with a Dominion, and c)they show a variety of real-world models of &quot;barbarian&quot;, including common ones the setting has lacked, such as invading refugees (ala the Goths).<br /> <br /> I'm now planning a Lunar game set in the North-East, which will briefly feature all the Northern Lunars mentioned (except maybe Smiling Rat, because he never gets invited to parties), and in which the PCs will have to grapple with the Empire of the Bear.<br /> <br /> But I guess fluff is, primarily, subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-06-2019, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T22:31:53-08:00","id":1294329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294311#post1294311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only person who saw italicized descriptors of Territories and thought &quot;Ooo, that suggests new mechanics to come.&quot;?<br /> Maybe lunar specific, or maybe not generalized mechanics for ruling a place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its stating the places with those descriptors have been claimed using Boundary-Marking Meditation and those are the traits the lunar patron assigned using the charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T00:41:32-08:00","id":1294337,"title":"","content":"Well, finally had a chance to get to their parts (I skipped ahead to Leviathan earlier to see what the preview left out) and Ma-Ha-Suchi actually now has a nation instead of squatting in a ruin full of idiot savage beastmen shitting in the corners (but somehow supporting an army) and Raksi's place actually sounds like a place sane people might consider livable instead of sounding like a nonstop lunatic carnival squatting on some ruins full of first age wonders (they even managed to maintain running water in homes this edition!). And the new ones I've gotten to so far are also interesting places I'd like to have characters visit. I do feel bad for True Voice, though. Finding out the hard way that if you go away for a few centuries and come back your society is going to have grown in ways you never intended and even starts doing things like interpreting your holy bear book in ways you didn't intend them to interpret the passages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T02:50:01-08:00","id":1294346,"title":"","content":"It made me think of the Dostoevsky story where Jesus comes back in 15th century Spain and is arrested for heresy by the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how True Voice has presented herself though; do they know she is 500 years old, or think she's just a regular Khoja?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:04:08-08:00","id":1294420,"title":"","content":"Reading <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1294417#post1294417\">Vance's comment</a> about the Bear Empire: &quot;I'm True Voice! <i>The </i>True Voice! Look, in the Book of the Bear, it is written that...&quot; and then she cites some verses she specifically dictated for the purpose of getting these folks to obey her when she returned.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, you may well be True Voice,&quot; a kindly young khoja says, &quot;but your interpretation of the Book of the Bear is somewhat lacking.&quot;<br /> <br /> Isn't this basically the same shtick The Silver Prince did in Onyx only somewhat less successful? I'm not pointing it out as a flaw or as a knock on the portrayal, at all. I find it interesting to see a take on &quot;I set up a prophecy that I'd return to lead a people and then come back to fulfill it&quot; where the society has moved on a bit since then and it doesn't quite work. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T11:19:36-08:00","id":1294458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294296#post1294296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have reached the words &quot;tame great flying eels&quot; and now my life is complete.<br /> <br /> And Aum-Ashatra is a surprisingly cool dude, I guess. He's no <i>great flying eel</i> though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I read it and thought of these guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.games-workshop.com/resources/catalog/product/920x950/99120219008_IdonethMorrsarrGuard01.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:06:37-08:00","id":1294470,"title":"","content":"Yeah... that looks pretty reasonable.<br /> <br /> Though those outfits don't look very sensible for the far(ish) north.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:15:33-08:00","id":1294473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294420#post1294420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1294417#post1294417&amp;quot;]Vance's</a> comment[/URL] about the Bear Empire: &amp;quot;I'm True Voice! <i>The </i>True Voice! Look, in the Book of the Bear, it is written that...&amp;quot; and then she cites some verses she specifically dictated for the purpose of getting these folks to obey her when she returned.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Ah, you may well be True Voice,&amp;quot; a kindly young khoja says, &amp;quot;but your interpretation of the Book of the Bear is somewhat lacking.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Isn't this basically the same shtick The Silver Prince did in Onyx only somewhat less successful? I'm not pointing it out as a flaw or as a knock on the portrayal, at all. I find it interesting to see a take on &amp;quot;I set up a prophecy that I'd return to lead a people and then come back to fulfill it&amp;quot; where the society has moved on a bit since then and it doesn't quite work. I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t know what the Silver Prince did in Onyx in 3E - save that in 3E he actually wants a society that unites the living and the dead and it\u2019s not just a cover for an apocalyptic doom fleet forged from the dead he pretends to socially promote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T17:06:45-08:00","id":1294542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294276#post1294276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it\u2019s not a good setting for Lunars because they\u2019re winning? Your assumption of \u201cfailing to take Castle Greyskull\u201d, precludes the most obvious Lunar Adventure path: push out the colonists once and for all and take Faxai as your own seat!</div> </div> </div> </div>No? I am not sure what your are even talking about.<br /> <br /> The issue I see is how are you going to stretch taking a single fortified port over the entire campaign? There is nothing else to do on the caul except try and push the realm out of a single settlement or speak with a bunch lunar generals who don't have anything interesting to say, and when you do finally push out the realm your prize is a mystery box of vague nothings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T18:25:54-08:00","id":1294554,"title":"","content":"Its not exactly hard for a ST to say 'prior to your arrival the Realm made a huge push to retake the island and reclaimed some of it' and have you break the back of that offensive and retake however many cities you want to retake before you deem your contribution 'worthy'. Its pretty important for Lunars to actually be able to demonstrate the fact that they are actively winning on some fronts so they don't feel like complete chumps in the base game but its trivially easy to undo it at your table if you want the glory of making a huge contribution to that particular theater of the conflict instead of coming in after others did most of the work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-06-2019, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:30:33-08:00","id":1294566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294554#post1294554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not exactly hard for a ST to say 'prior to your arrival the Realm made a huge push to retake the island and reclaimed some of it' and have you break the back of that offensive and retake however many cities you want to retake before you deem your contribution 'worthy'. Its pretty important for Lunars to actually be able to demonstrate the fact that they are actively winning on some fronts so they don't feel like complete chumps in the base game but its trivially easy to undo it at your table if you want the glory of making a huge contribution to that particular theater of the conflict instead of coming in after others did most of the work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but you can do that literally anywhere else in creation. The issue isn't that lunars are winning the issue is that they don't have anything to do while winning. Dynasts get to &quot;win&quot; across the greatest empire in creation and have a huge number of intersting plot hooks that tie into being scions of the realm. In the caul all lunars have is partaking in a siege of one city of a a unknown time period for a undefined reward. Lunars have almost unfettered access to 90 percent of the caul and they can do literally nothing with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:13:11-08:00","id":1294586,"title":"","content":"Honestly, there is still stuff to do you just don't have it handed to you on a platter. Maybe you find out the secret language of men that was traded to end a famine was actually vital to keeping it anchored in reality and have to do things to rediscover and spread it before the whole place vanishes like a waking dream, for example. Its just most likely going to be weird stuff because the Caul is a weird place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:23:54-08:00","id":1294590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294586#post1294586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, there is still stuff to do you just don't have it handed to you on a platter. Maybe you find out the secret language of men that was traded to end a famine was actually vital to keeping it anchored in reality and have to do things to rediscover and spread it before the whole place vanishes like a waking dream, for example. Its just most likely going to be weird stuff because the Caul is a weird place.</div> </div> </div> </div>And once again what does this have to do with the caul? I could create a entirely new setting from scratch and then write the caul at the top, it's what you have to do with huge swaths of the map and there is nothing wrong with.<br /> <br /> With the caul though I felt like the idea was for a more focused and detailed game. A chance to try something you may not think of in other parts of creation. The Dragonblooded POV delivers this in spades while I personally feel the lunar POV does not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:51:31-08:00","id":1294598,"title":"","content":"Well, if it makes you feel better there is other stuff to do in the West. Spear-Empress Bhadri from the write up for The Bronze Tide seems like a pretty big threat that might expand out into a danger to the whole region and her only current 'opposition' is a bunch of people saying 'nope nope nope' and running away while raiding people in their retreat path for supplies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:04:42-08:00","id":1294602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294590#post1294590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And once again what does this have to do with the caul? I could create a entirely new setting from scratch and then write the caul at the top, it's what you have to do with huge swaths of the map and there is nothing wrong with.<br /> <br /> With the caul though I felt like the idea was for a more focused and detailed game. A chance to try something you may not think of in other parts of creation. The Dragonblooded POV delivers this in spades while I personally feel the lunar POV does not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can't think of anything unique to do with a literal living continent? One that can explicitly interfere, and does, with people who displease it?<br /> <br /> Even if it's just a home base for Lunars, trying to understand the mysteries of the often mercurial child of Gaia and Luna seems like a fine subplot. There, the story is just as much about the land as a very present character in any story, and trying to communicate and placate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:32:15-08:00","id":1294716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294602#post1294602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can't think of anything unique to do with a literal living continent? One that can explicitly interfere, and does, with people who displease it?<br /> <br /> Even if it's just a home base for Lunars, trying to understand the mysteries of the often mercurial child of Gaia and Luna seems like a fine subplot. There, the story is just as much about the land as a very present character in any story, and trying to communicate and placate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could but I am not one of the writers and I do not see a very strong selling point to be &quot;well sure it doesn't work but I am selling you this duct tape and all this old junk so you can just do it yourself right?&quot; I would much prefer it worked right out of the gate instead of having to kludge it together myself.<br /> <br /> Speaking personally another thing against the Caul is really just that it is eating word count in a already weak chapter. Like the Core book presented Dominions as the 10 000 fangs of the silver pact that encircle and harry the realm and almost none of them live up to that ideal.<br /> <br /> 1. The spider king is at &quot;war&quot; with the realm but is effectively just a bandit whose most pressing problems are food shortages and managing immigration.<br /> 2. Skhandar-Bal is not at war with the realm but maybe in like 50 years? who knows.<br /> 3. The Touman clans are also not at war with the realm but like any day now they might be I swear.<br /> 4. Iscomay is basically just the realm lite because it turns out lunars are not so good at this whole people management thing and ended up losing control completely. So four dominions in and Lunars have managed to unintentionally create more imperialist powers than they have hindered.<br /> 5. Ma ha suchi is not at war with the realm because he is tired of getting his ass kicked and so sits and sulks.<br /> 6. The bronze tide did not go to war with the realm and in fact never will since that would take away too much time from being GOT wildlings running from the white walkers.<br /> 7. The caul is at war with the realm but as stated before there is nothing interesting to do there so I would basically have to create an entirely new dominion and then slap the word caul at the top.<br /> 8. Mahalanka, luthe and the eskari are at war with the realm but this is still only 3 out of 10 spotlighted dominions. Two of which are only important because they have a 1000's year old first age elder there.<br /> <br /> Like one of the strengths of WFHW was that it really hammered home the idea that the empire is full of interesting NPC's doing their own things but it was still a time of tumult and a bunch of young dynasts could make a difference one way or another.<br /> <br /> The dominions chapters should of been something I could point players to as examples of cool things lunars can do but it is filled with stuff they either can't do because they are not E6 elders with a 1000 years or prep or stuff they don't want to do because it would mean being a weird ineffectual uncle trying to convince random people its in their best interest to throw themselves against the imperial meat grinder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:47:17-08:00","id":1294718,"title":"","content":"Just raised my donation to the $130 level - I am now a Champion of the Silver Pact! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:19:32-08:00","id":1294726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294716#post1294716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could but I am not one of the writers and I do not see a very strong selling point to be &quot;well sure it doesn't work but I am selling you this duct tape and all this old junk so you can just do it yourself right?&quot; I would much prefer it worked right out of the gate instead of having to kludge it together myself.<br /> <br /> Speaking personally another thing against the Caul is really just that it is eating word count in a already weak chapter. Like the Core book presented Dominions as the 10 000 fangs of the silver pact that encircle and harry the realm and almost none of them live up to that ideal.<br /> <br /> 1. The spider king is at &quot;war&quot; with the realm but is effectively just a bandit whose most pressing problems are food shortages and managing immigration.<br /> 2. Skhandar-Bal is not at war with the realm but maybe in like 50 years? who knows.<br /> 3. The Touman clans are also not at war with the realm but like any day now they might be I swear.<br /> 4. Iscomay is basically just the realm lite because it turns out lunars are not so good at this whole people management thing and ended up losing control completely. So four dominions in and Lunars have managed to unintentionally create more imperialist powers than they have hindered.<br /> 5. Ma ha suchi is not at war with the realm because he is tired of getting his ass kicked and so sits and sulks.<br /> 6. The bronze tide did not go to war with the realm and in fact never will since that would take away too much time from being GOT wildlings running from the white walkers.<br /> 7. The caul is at war with the realm but as stated before there is nothing interesting to do there so I would basically have to create an entirely new dominion and then slap the word caul at the top.<br /> 8. Mahalanka, luthe and the eskari are at war with the realm but this is still only 3 out of 10 spotlighted dominions. Two of which are only important because they have a 1000's year old first age elder there.<br /> <br /> Like one of the strengths of WFHW was that it really hammered home the idea that the empire is full of interesting NPC's doing their own things but it was still a time of tumult and a bunch of young dynasts could make a difference one way or another.<br /> <br /> The dominions chapters should of been something I could point players to as examples of cool things lunars can do but it is filled with stuff they either can't do because they are not E6 elders with a 1000 years or prep or stuff they don't want to do because it would mean being a weird ineffectual uncle trying to convince random people its in their best interest to throw themselves against the imperial meat grinder.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to point out that one criticism of the Silver Pact chapter was that it seemed like Lunars are utterly obsessed with fighting the Realm. Realm, Realm, Realm, that's all it seemed to be.<br /> <br /> (And, in fact, the very first two words of the Dominion chapter are &quot;The Realm's&quot;)<br /> <br /> So the Dominions chapter presents a number of Lunar-influenced societies which present a number of different models of interaction with the Realm - war, piracy, raiding, blocking, thinking about war, or completely ignoring it.<br /> <br /> If your main objective for the Dominions chapter is &quot;How does it show the Lunars awesomely fighting the Realm?&quot; then, yeah, it's actually not that great.<br /> <br /> But I actually wasn't that interested in that, and I really liked it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I didn't like the Silver Pact chapter as I found an entire chapter of fighting the Realm... not bad, per-se, but not that exciting. Whereas I guess you preferred it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:27:16-08:00","id":1294768,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2438987\" target=\"_blank\">Final sample Charms ahead of tomorrow.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:49:05-08:00","id":1294774,"title":"","content":"So lunars can be Alucard and sacrifice a stolen face to have it eat their death for them. Though they can't spam it because its only once per story and getting 'killed' still puts them out of commission for awhile in a state that appears identical to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:53:43-08:00","id":1294776,"title":"","content":"Also, 240K stretch goal reached now we get info on Luna's court and that new initiation. Also new stretch goals revealed, at 255k Many Faced Strangers gets colored art, 260k we get the dominion of that necromancy leopard and his pal (great personal interest to me), and 270K we get Sublime Danger's write up as well as the martial art she has mastered that gives her sword wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:13:48-08:00","id":1294784,"title":"","content":"Necromancy leopard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:19:16-08:00","id":1294785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294768#post1294768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2438987\" target=\"_blank\">Final sample Charms ahead of tomorrow.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the wits charms are way better persona charms. Minimal but really distinct changes that don't require multiple sheets or tracking extra XP or making starting characters who are just plain barely functioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:47:10-08:00","id":1294794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294784#post1294784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necromancy leopard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven Obsidian Leopard, a necromancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:59:00-08:00","id":1294811,"title":"","content":"Quick question about a charm, I'll ask the Devs if there's no easy answer here:<br /> Moonlight Curtain Drawn and its upgrade Argent Deceiver Smile: when do I pay for Argent Deceiver Smile and how long does it last? Is it activates when you activate MCD and last for the duration or every time you want to use the effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:23:21-08:00","id":1294822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294811#post1294811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moonlight Curtain Drawn and its upgrade Argent Deceiver Smile: when do I pay for Argent Deceiver Smile and how long does it last? Is it activates when you activate MCD and last for the duration or every time you want to use the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd rule the latter - basically, as long as Moonlight Curtain Drawn is active, every time your Guile would apply against an attempt to detect your lies or determine your intent to deceive, you can spend 2 motes right then to get the +3 boost. But if someone tries to read you again later in the scene, you'll have to pay another 2 motes for the same bonus to apply.<br /> <br /> My logic is basically that it's better balanced that way. 5m total is pretty cheap to get +3 Guile for a whole scene for all attempts to lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T16:57:39-08:00","id":1294925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294726#post1294726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to point out that one criticism of the Silver Pact chapter was that it seemed like Lunars are utterly obsessed with fighting the Realm. Realm, Realm, Realm, that's all it seemed to be.<br /> <br /> (And, in fact, the very first two words of the Dominion chapter are &quot;The Realm's&quot;)<br /> <br /> So the Dominions chapter presents a number of Lunar-influenced societies which present a number of different models of interaction with the Realm - war, piracy, raiding, blocking, thinking about war, or completely ignoring it.<br /> <br /> If your main objective for the Dominions chapter is &quot;How does it show the Lunars awesomely fighting the Realm?&quot; then, yeah, it's actually not that great.<br /> <br /> But I actually wasn't that interested in that, and I really liked it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I didn't like the Silver Pact chapter as I found an entire chapter of fighting the Realm... not bad, per-se, but not that exciting. Whereas I guess you preferred it?</div> </div> </div> </div>My main objection is the caul is a waste of word count from the lunar POV, whether they are fighting the realm or the snow leopards doesn't really matter. My secondary concern that is exacerbating my first is that most the dominions are not supporting the thesis laid down in chapter 2.<br /> <br /> its not a matter of liking or disliking the focus on the realm only that I want some consistency on it. WFHW had a single central game point and that was the realm civil war. FATG is splitting focus between lunars fighting a eternal war against the realm and lunars fucking around the threshold and both ideas are suffering for it. I don't prefer one over the other but they should of picked one and ran with it instead of waffling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T17:07:25-08:00","id":1294927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294925#post1294925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My main objection is the caul is a waste of word count from the lunar POV, whether they are fighting the realm or the snow leopards doesn't really matter. My secondary concern that is exacerbating my first is that most the dominions are not supporting the thesis laid down in chapter 2.<br /> <br /> its not a matter of liking or disliking the focus on the realm only that I want some consistency on it. WFHW had a single central game point and that was the realm civil war. FATG is splitting focus between lunars fighting a eternal war against the realm and lunars fucking around the threshold and both ideas are suffering for it. I don't prefer one over the other but they should of picked one and ran with it instead of waffling.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue is that you can have both but only if the silver pack isn't as cohesive as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T22:36:40-08:00","id":1294974,"title":"","content":"Why not? /10ch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T23:04:07-08:00","id":1294976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294927#post1294927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is that you can have both but only if the silver pack isn't as cohesive as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silver Pact is incredibly non-cohesive. That\u2019s how it\u2019s as all encompassing as it is- by being an EXTREMELY loose association that tattooed Lunars are basically assumed part of unless they actively choose otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T01:27:14-08:00","id":1294996,"title":"","content":"The Silver Pact ...really isn't particularly cohesive. It's a group of 400ish people, most of whom generally agree on two things:<br /> <br /> 1) The Realm and Sidereals need to go down!<br /> <br /> 2) We shouldn't kill each other and, by extension, we shouldn't let the Realm kill us.<br /> <br /> Everything else is up for debate, petty politicking, and so on.<br /> <br /> And... I guess I feel like that comes across fairly well here to me. Each place has a Lunar who is doing their own thing and might be inclined to help with your thing, but they could use a favor or two in return or some persuading or whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here, let's see what we can see as regards each one dealing with the Realm, if you're playing as Pact Lunars:<br /> <br /> 1) Mountain of the Spider King: a Lunar ruler uses his well defended home to deny a valuable trade route to the Realm and help others. However, the help he freely gives can get stretched at times, so if you could find a way to increase their food supply, they would likely be inclined to help you out. (Maybe you could get True Voice to help him out with some geomancy for the right price?). There's also a nearby Realm outpost that's trying to keep the sea trade route open. If you can break that place in half, that will end Realm trade in the area for years. Or maybe just help fund the pirates.<br /> <br /> 2) Skandhar-Bhal: Not!Shangi-la where an ancient Lunar retired from the world, sickened by violence. However, said Lunar has been training a formidable fighting force ...but one that has not seen any actual fighting beyond what others would consider a bar rroom brawl or minor skirmish. The Lunar considers coming back to the world and bringing these troops to war, but are they really ready? Can you help them become ready? Should you convince them to stay where they are?<br /> <br /> 3) The Touman Clans. This place has a proud tradition of raiding others but some want to remain in this very nice city they've claimed and start building an empire. Their Lunar cohort is thinking about trying to get them to go on the road again with her and some of the people would like it. Can you tip the balance one way or another?<br /> <br /> 4) The Empire of the Bear: I built this place to fight the Realm and now they don't want to. So, anyone up for toppling a small government before we topple the big one? But, really, helping Truce Voice retake control of this empire and send it against the Realm is going to be a job and a half. Alternately reforming it to be less evil and/or unlikely to implode due to Janissary revolts in a few decades is a thing you could try that might be more doable? Maybe you could take part of the army and go conquer the nearest Satrapy so you can lower taxes or something.<br /> <br /> 5) Nameless Lair: This place is why the Realm and Prasad are two different nations instead of one bigger one. They also lead irregular raids on outsiders and Realm Satrapies, all the more troubling for their apparent randomness. And Ma-Ha-Suchi is there to be negotiated with, approached for resources, and so on.<br /> <br /> 6) Mahalanka. It's Raksi. She is a source of knowledge and power. Her empire is strong. When she thinks the time is right, she will pour over the Realm's eastern satrapies like a wave. Until then, none would dare attack her.<br /> <br /> 7) The Eskari are a nomadic people that a Lunar is turning into a horde of raiders who will attack the Realm's southern trade and satrapies. Pretty straightforward. You can get involved in planning this or try to get them to target a particular place.<br /> <br /> 8) The Bronze Tide, if one could treat with Lukha Palash and his council, might be turned away from their conquering of the Isles and put towards the destruction of Realm fleets or the besieging of Faxai. There is likely much they would do if you could present them the broken heart of of Bhadri. With some cleverness one might even use the Tide to turn the Spear-Empress against another hated enemy and let two problems solve each other.<br /> <br /> 9) Luthe. Leviathan has a nice city here.and with his new motivation, it's going on a war footing. There will be lots of issues to iron out along the way that one can help with or one can just ride along on raids against Realm shipping.<br /> <br /> 10) The Caul. We'll be getting a full chapter as a how to book for doing this later on, but, now, let's start with murdering every non-native who sets foot outside Faxai, infiltrating the city to find out more about the local DBs, air dropping firebombs, cutting off shipping, and so on.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I see plenty there for stuff to work with for going against the Realm. It may not all be perfectly obvious, but the Realm is present in most of them, in one way or another. They're also all interesting places to be from and each has some kind of crisis that could be meddled with. <br /> <br /> I think they all work just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:23:09-08:00","id":1295033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294785#post1294785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the wits charms are way better persona charms. Minimal but really distinct changes that don't require multiple sheets or tracking extra XP or making starting characters who are just plain barely functioning.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends.<br /> The Solar persona charms frontload their complexity by treating the new self as a different character. This charm + the general one for physical attributes redistribute attribute dots and allows you to purchase charms that are only usable when you meet their prerequisites, which is fine as long as you're accurately recording the charms you can't always use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T08:02:04-08:00","id":1295046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295033#post1295033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends.<br /> The Solar persona charms frontload their complexity by treating the new self as a different character. This charm + the general one for physical attributes redistribute attribute dots and allows you to purchase charms that are only usable when you meet their prerequisites, which is fine as long as you're accurately recording the charms you can't always use.</div> </div> </div> </div>A persona is also hugely understated even outside of CC. the persona can't do much more than one or two functions. Personally, I think solar persona should just excises the extra character sheets you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:34:08-08:00","id":1295092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1294822#post1294822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5m total is pretty cheap to get +3 Guile for a whole scene for all attempts to lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>So\u2019s 4m for +3 Guile for all purposes indefinitely (Guarded Thoughts Meditation), that sounds like a perfectly balanced Lunar version to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:45:32-08:00","id":1295096,"title":"","content":"Well, a high stamina lunar focused on not dying charms is <i>ridiculously</i> hard to kill. If they get the cap stone charm for that charm tree they don't even die when they are killed regardless of how they are killed (asked and it was dev confirmed that even something like reducing them to ash wont stop them from coming back).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T19:40:07-08:00","id":1295183,"title":"","content":"I feel bad for the unlucky Lunar that gets Mountain-Burden Stone as their expression-of-self Radiant Basilisc Jewel hearthstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T20:08:30-08:00","id":1295196,"title":"","content":"Lunars have a charm that lets them teach Sorcery to their dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T20:34:56-08:00","id":1295202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295096#post1295096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a high stamina lunar focused on not dying charms is <i>ridiculously</i> hard to kill. If they get the cap stone charm for that charm tree they don't even die when they are killed regardless of how they are killed (asked and it was dev confirmed that even something like reducing them to ash wont stop them from coming back).</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we know how Sha\u2019a Ok\u2019a does it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T22:10:12-08:00","id":1295214,"title":"","content":"I think I might prefer the charm that turns me into a being of legendary size over deadly beastman transformation if I decide to transform to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T22:27:45-08:00","id":1295217,"title":"","content":"Does Dog-Tongue Method or equivalent no longer exist?<br /> <br /> I can't find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:51:54-08:00","id":1295230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295217#post1295217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Dog-Tongue Method or equivalent no longer exist?<br /> <br /> I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instinctive Unity Approach is the closest analogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:57:34-08:00","id":1295233,"title":"","content":"Ah, so just being friends with animals, not talking to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:58:36-08:00","id":1295304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295233#post1295233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so just being friends with animals, not talking to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC back when they did the core a generic &quot;talks to animals&quot; power was deemed to have the same basic problem as being able to interrogate least gods. <br /> Either-<br /> A. You model them as people and have an unparalleled advantage at gathering information.<br /> B. Try to portray animal intellect which will vary wildly from Storyteller to Storyteller, to the point that you might end up paying xp for the priviledge of having annoying circular conversations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T07:19:04-08:00","id":1295306,"title":"","content":"But those ridiculous conversations were so fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Oh well, never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T08:24:36-08:00","id":1295319,"title":"","content":"The real issue is the the sheer scope of animals. Having distinct \u201cbeast tongues\u201d that can be gained through sorcery or divine blessing doesn\u2019t have the same &quot;I sweep the room for tiny insects and micro organisms who might be listening in on us!&quot; problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T09:56:12-08:00","id":1295335,"title":"","content":"Hmm, its starting to look like we might not get to the current 270K finish line in terms of stretch goals. It will be too bad if we miss out on that awesome martial art that lets you have sword wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:06:43-08:00","id":1295343,"title":"","content":"Things tend to accelerate a bit over the last few days of the KS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T10:09:18-08:00","id":1295344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295335#post1295335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, its starting to look like we might not get to the current 270K finish line in terms of stretch goals. It will be too bad if we miss out on that awesome martial art that lets you have sword wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's usually a significant uptick in the final few days - WFHW got 54K and 300-odd backers in its last four days. I wouldn't be worried on breaking 270K, even with Fangs' lower average pledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T17:40:01-08:00","id":1295419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295335#post1295335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, its starting to look like we might not get to the current 270K finish line in terms of stretch goals. It will be too bad if we miss out on that awesome martial art that lets you have sword wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn\u2019t. We will absolutely hit that. The stretch will be making a run for 300k.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T18:57:02-08:00","id":1295436,"title":"","content":"Obviously they should put some Lunar-themed warstriders* at 300k to take advantage of our desperation to not miss that one again. XD<br /> <br /> * Read: Zoids. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T19:19:24-08:00","id":1295441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295419#post1295419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it isn\u2019t. We will absolutely hit that. The stretch will be making a run for 300k.</div> </div> </div> </div>Past success doesn't foretell future endeavors. There are unique barriers to Lunars that Dragon Blooded did not. First among them high international shipping. I do hope I am wrong but a pessimistic view has its benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T19:34:41-08:00","id":1295445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295217#post1295217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Dog-Tongue Method or equivalent no longer exist?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295230#post1295230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instinctive Unity Approach is the closest analogue.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295233#post1295233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so just being friends with animals, not talking to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, not talking <i>as</i> animals.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Animal Shapes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her ability to communicate is limited by the animal\u2019s anatomy. Most are incapable of speaking human languages, forcing her to rely on body language and whatever noises she can make.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess it comes down to how generous your storyteller interprets anatomy that allows human speech...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-09-2019, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:03:15-08:00","id":1295451,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the lack of Dog-Tongue Method or equivalent is a deliberate choice meant to ... I don't know, I really don't even know why it isn't there, but I wonder if it's deliberate or if it's an oversight. It's definitely the first thing I'd ask for with a custom charm backer reward, but that would still mean that a basic utility Charm is in the companion and not the main Lunar book itself, which is going to upset people. <br /> <br /> I really don't understand, it's not like talking animals aren't present in the mythical and pop-cultural inspirations for Lunars, and it's a basic player utility that keeps the game fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:13:53-08:00","id":1295453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295451#post1295451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the lack of Dog-Tongue Method or equivalent is a deliberate choice meant to ... I don't know, I really don't even know why it isn't there, but I wonder if it's deliberate or if it's an oversight. It's definitely the first thing I'd ask for with a custom charm backer reward, but that would still mean that a basic utility Charm is in the companion and not the main Lunar book itself, which is going to upset people.<br /> <br /> I really don't understand, it's not like talking animals aren't present in the mythical and pop-cultural inspirations for Lunars, and it's a basic player utility that keeps the game fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instinctive Unity Approach fills its role of facilitating communications with animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:27:46-08:00","id":1295459,"title":"","content":"I would say some method for Lunars to be able to hold conversations with each other while they're all in animal form would be nice. Yes, there's Glance Oration Technique, but that has a duration of instant and 3m per couple of sentences can add up quickly if you're trying to hold a long conversation.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, right. Perfect Symmetry reduces its cost to zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 03-09-2019, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:34:08-08:00","id":1295462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295459#post1295459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say some method for Lunars to be able to hold conversations with each other while they're all in animal form would be nice. Yes, there's Glance Oration Technique, but that has a duration of instant and 3m per couple of sentences can add up quickly if you're trying to hold a long conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still use animal communication and body language. It's not much for debating politics, but it'll handle rudimentary communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:53:07-08:00","id":1295468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295453#post1295453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instinctive Unity Approach fills its role of facilitating communications with animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misread, it\u2019s not about talking to animals, it\u2019s about being a talking animal. Really-good-body-language-ing animals just aren\u2019t the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T21:07:00-08:00","id":1295474,"title":"","content":"Yeah, with all the talking animals in folklore etc it's just really odd that we can't use human mouth-words in animal form this edition, even with magic. With all the magical feats of shapeshifting and trickery Lunars are capable of it seems like an obvious gap in their capabilities. <br /> <br /> Plus I'm really attached to some of the roleplaying moments that have been enabled by that Charm in the past, so I'd hate to see it go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T00:05:25-08:00","id":1295515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295441#post1295441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Past success doesn't foretell future endeavors. There are unique barriers to Lunars that Dragon Blooded did not. First among them high international shipping. I do hope I am wrong but a pessimistic view has its benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most KSes have an 'inverted bell curve' of funding, with the two periods that usually see the highest rate of funding at the beginning and end (the end in large part because of Kickstarter's 72-hour notification). There will be a surge, the question is how much. Even just a bump up to 5k a day for Monday through Thursday (from 3-3.5k) would get us to Sublime Danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"h