 a bump up to 5k a day for Monday through Thursday (from 3-3.5k) would get us to Sublime Danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been doing something like 5k a day already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:30:22-07:00","id":1295580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295579#post1295579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've been doing something like 5k a day already.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/#chart-daily\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/023/972/157/3f553b9dda80d60e8533674ee31a8567_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-1.1.0&amp;crop=faces&amp;w=160&amp;h=90&amp;fit=crop&amp;v=1549138749&amp;auto=format&amp;frame=1&amp;q=92&amp;s=7d98a62f88e5f47818ba76d33e115473\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/#chart-daily\" target=\"_blank\"> Lunars: Fangs at the Gate for Exalted 3rd Ed. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/#chart-daily\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/#chart-daily </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A deluxe supplement detailing the Lunar Exalted for the Exalted 3rd Edition tabletop RPG </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T15:07:25-07:00","id":1295662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295468#post1295468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you misread, it\u2019s not about talking to animals, it\u2019s about being a talking animal. Really-good-body-language-ing animals just aren\u2019t the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked about a possibility for this on the new Ask Devs thread, and Vance agreed that making inherent human traits into mutations that can be applied to animal forms with Perfect Hybrid Interaction is a viable option. So just make human speech a 1 or 2 dot mutation. Much more cost effective than dedicating a Charm for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T17:53:15-07:00","id":1295701,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking human speech is a 2 dot merit<br /> <br /> Opposable Digits (allowing tool use and climbing that might be impossible in a given animal form) at 4 dots<br /> <br /> Biped (allows hand usage while also moving, and greater reach) - 2 points, Opposable Digits prerequisite","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-10-2019, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T18:53:29-07:00","id":1295714,"title":"","content":"I'd merge those two into a single Merit, rated (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022). Two dots nets you opposable digits, like on a chameleon's feet or raccoon's paws, coupled with awkward raccoon bipedalism, while four dots grants a full bipedal gait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T19:18:49-07:00","id":1295718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295714#post1295714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd merge those two into a single Merit, rated (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022). Two dots nets you opposable digits, like on a chameleon's feet or raccoon's paws, coupled with awkward raccoon bipedalism, while four dots grants a full bipedal gait.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the 2 dot version would let you pick up/hold/carry things, but not fine manipulation ala the 4 dot version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T07:11:52-07:00","id":1295802,"title":"","content":"255K art upgrade achieved","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:25:27-07:00","id":1295849,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2442815\" target=\"_blank\">Sample of the final chapter</a>, with a look at 3e Lilith and some of Creation's animals.<br /> <br /> Beyond Sublime Danger, 280k gives us stat blocks for Sha'a Oka's lieutenants, and 290k gives us another novella.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:35:46-07:00","id":1295850,"title":"","content":"So it looks like they kept the basic concept of Lilith and just wrote Desus out entirely. Probably sensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:53:50-07:00","id":1295857,"title":"","content":"RIP Desus, you were such a dick you were retconned out of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:03:35-07:00","id":1295861,"title":"","content":"Ding Dong Desus' Gone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:36:36-07:00","id":1295868,"title":"","content":"You used to be memorable, HeartBrokenMaiden#35492573498. You used to mean something, you stood as an example of how bad Solar mind fuckery could get. Now, you are utterly forgettable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:46:07-07:00","id":1295870,"title":"","content":"The new write-up for Lilith is pretty good. Between returning to her original concept, and painting her retreat from the world as the ramifications of a demigod dealing with long and deep grief over an even longer-lasting genuine relationship with her Solar bondmate, her backstory is very emotionally palpable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T11:30:39-07:00","id":1295880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295870#post1295870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new write-up for Lilith is pretty good. Between returning to her original concept, and painting her retreat from the world as the ramifications of a demigod dealing with long and deep grief over an even longer-lasting genuine relationship with her Solar bondmate, her backstory is very emotionally palpable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heavily disagree. This is my problem with Ma-Ha-Suchi. It's an entirely different character from past editions and while I thought 2e went entirely too far in one direction this goes heavily in the opposite direction. She's named lilith but it's only in name and if it's only in name you might as well name her something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T11:44:49-07:00","id":1295882,"title":"","content":"I think it does return to 1st edition; but, essentially, I don't really see her as a character with whom there's a lot interesting to do, compared to other Elders. Either in 3rd or 1st.<br /> <br /> I've used Ma-Ha-Suchi in games, I've used Raksi in games, I've never used Lilith. The fact her ex has a different name and isn't an abuser doesn't really change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-11-2019, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T11:53:55-07:00","id":1295885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295870#post1295870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new write-up for Lilith is pretty good. Between returning to her original concept, and painting her retreat from the world as the ramifications of a demigod dealing with long and deep grief over an even longer-lasting genuine relationship with her Solar bondmate, her backstory is very emotionally palpable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could not agree more.<br /> <br /> Folks tend to forget this but we have historical had next to no actual canon example of a healthy Solar Bond, and books are in part supposed to create and inspiration framework. Second edition doubled down on this so much that it made no pair but two in my memory anything remotely resembling something to be mourned (in large part due to their not being heavily built on), meanwhile I can think of at least a dozen First Age Solars who were rape-hungry monsters (which was weirdly enough not tied to the Flaw of any of the examples that got a stat block, making you wonder if Sol was purposely picking rapists). It made one splat monsters and the other victims as a default.<br /> <br /> This new version of Lilith is a good indicator of the new direction for Lunars as a whole, she is very much the exception among the elders we have access to in her mourning while also telling the reader that at least <i>some </i>Lunars remember their time with their supposed soul-bound comrades well. The framing is also very different, with it being in the context of being worn-down by her grief after a long time with different agendas, lovers and causes before finally choosing to rest, which is a stark contrast to the beaten victim that fled Creation and cared little for her kin of past editions.<br /> <br /> I'm sort of inclined to refer to the Lost Lenore trope from the way the recollections are referred to. Actually, depending on how you read her time as an Owl, I'd be sort of inclined to almost start looking towards a Don Quixote character (its reaching but its also fun).<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that a good book sort of gives you a good reference for a wide array of things. Most of the Shahan-yas are thankfully disconnected from Solars altogether, some historical Solars had outright antagonistic relationships and the bond is really only shown in present terms in three Shahan-yas. Sublime from her line gives you a good Shounen-rival angle, Leviathan gives you a 'moved on' angle, while Lilith gives a 'this was a good thing I want back in my life' angle.<br /> <br /> Which is a site better than past editions wherein the Solar Bond was shown to Lunar Players as rape, abuse and literal mind-wiping (recall that one Lunar that got turned into breeding octopus when his mate went extra-crazy?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T11:54:20-07:00","id":1295886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295868#post1295868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You used to be memorable, HeartBrokenMaiden#35492573498. You used to mean something, you stood as an example of how bad Solar mind fuckery could get. Now, you are utterly forgettable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if 'a collection of every battered wife trope in fiction' is very 'unique'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:10:18-07:00","id":1295892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295886#post1295886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if 'a collection of every battered wife trope in fiction' is very 'unique'</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said unique, I just said she was memorable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:25:06-07:00","id":1295898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295882#post1295882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does return to 1st edition; but, essentially, I don't really see her as a character with whom there's a lot interesting to do, compared to other Elders. Either in 3rd or 1st.<br /> <br /> I've used Ma-Ha-Suchi in games, I've used Raksi in games, I've never used Lilith. The fact her ex has a different name and isn't an abuser doesn't really change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it but I don't think they should have named a completely different character with old character names. Either use lilith for the most part or just call her something else. My issue with this is that it seemed like originally lilith had a healthy relationship that degraded as the solars got mad. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm kind of shocked at how many lunars seem okay with solars or at least neutral which I guess means that in this edition lunars just didn't care about what wrong doing solars were doing to justify the usurpation kind of attacking them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:35:41-07:00","id":1295902,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that for a lot of these characters, 1E presented them a certain way, then 2E destroyed their characterization and warped it to fit what it wanted, presumably for shock value or otherwise just because they were there. In such a case, it's not really correct to go with a brand new character, a lot of these characters are well known, and returning them to their 1E roots isn't betraying them, rather I'd suggest brutally and totally changing them between 1st and 2nd was the significant change.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how exactly she's portrayed, an edition of Exalted without Raksi would be as weird as one without Attributes and Abilities at this point, and if she wasn't written up people would just go with old information and assume it's still true, and then we play a game of telephone that ends with the prior edition information becoming the fanon that people are introduced to as being strictly the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:39:41-07:00","id":1295904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295882#post1295882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does return to 1st edition; but, essentially, I don't really see her as a character with whom there's a lot interesting to do, compared to other Elders. Either in 3rd or 1st.<br /> <br /> I've used Ma-Ha-Suchi in games, I've used Raksi in games, I've never used Lilith. The fact her ex has a different name and isn't an abuser doesn't really change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lilith has never quite been able to escape being a broad archetype that people make their own &quot;ex-wife from another life&quot; based on her and then it only stands to reason that they prefer their own work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:41:28-07:00","id":1295905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295902#post1295902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is that for a lot of these characters, 1E presented them a certain way, then 2E destroyed their characterization and warped it to fit what it wanted, presumably for shock value or otherwise just because they were there. In such a case, it's not really correct to go with a brand new character, a lot of these characters are well known, and returning them to their 1E roots isn't betraying them, rather I'd suggest brutally and totally changing them between 1st and 2nd was the significant change.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how exactly she's portrayed, an edition of Exalted without Raksi would be as weird as one without Attributes and Abilities at this point, and if she wasn't written up people would just go with old information and assume it's still true, and then we play a game of telephone that ends with the prior edition information becoming the fanon that people are introduced to as being strictly the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel like Raksi was mostly fine but would prefer the fact if she liked the taste of babies for real instead of as a trick. However, I do think that a number of them were portrayed so radically different that it would be better to just change them where as 2E just kind of made them more edger than they used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:54:10-07:00","id":1295909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295868#post1295868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You used to be memorable, HeartBrokenMaiden#35492573498. You used to mean something, you stood as an example of how bad Solar mind fuckery could get. Now, you are utterly forgettable.</div> </div> </div> </div>A major Lunar character should not stand as an example of something about Solars.<br /> <br /> Lilith didn\u2019t need Desus to be memorable when she was first introduced in 1E chapter fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-11-2019, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:17:08-07:00","id":1295916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is a site better than past editions wherein the Solar Bond was shown to Lunar Players as rape, abuse and literal mind-wiping (recall that one Lunar that got turned into breeding octopus when his mate went extra-crazy?). </div> </div> </div>Don't remember that one, which book was it in? One of the First Age books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:26:59-07:00","id":1295921,"title":"","content":"Can't believe we have 2 pages of Lilith discussion and no one's mentioned seeing our first example of an Essence 6 Elder Exalted charm. It's a great example of a subtle and specific power that's unique to them. It doesn't send cities into hell, but it would be very useful for someone in her position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:32:30-07:00","id":1295922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295916#post1295916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't remember that one, which book was it in? One of the First Age books?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the Western Section of Lands of Creation, pg. 125.<br /> <br /> Although there are alot of others aside from K'tula, its pretty tricky to find any Solar that isnt a total monster or a Lunar who has anything resembling a positive bond in that book by my reading (Jackal and the Co-Ruler of Whitewall, maybe Shining Ocelot but he was arguably as crazy as his wife).<br /> <br /> Its very nice with 3ed that the Bond is no longer a really bad taste in the mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:35:18-07:00","id":1295924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295921#post1295921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't believe we have 2 pages of Lilith discussion and no one's mentioned seeing our first example of an Essence 6 Elder Exalted charm. It's a great example of a subtle and specific power that's unique to them. It doesn't send cities into hell, but it would be very useful for someone in her position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a very cool charm really, what it does is also very fun and lets an ST use it to explain really cool set interactions with trickster mentors by my mileage. Not 100% on it being E6, but still very cool!<br /> <br /> I wonder if any of the other elders will have similarly unique/potent charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:13:49-07:00","id":1295950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295921#post1295921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't believe we have 2 pages of Lilith discussion and no one's mentioned seeing our first example of an Essence 6 Elder Exalted charm. It's a great example of a subtle and specific power that's unique to them. It doesn't send cities into hell, but it would be very useful for someone in her position.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm wondering why it's presented in the style of a PC option, and not a QC Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:27:06-07:00","id":1295952,"title":"","content":"So, reading that one it says that he got turned into a mindless tentacle monster by a lab accident and the grief turned her into a crazy transhumanist who turned herself into a tentacle monster and says being a cephalopod abomination is a good thing to make herself feel better about accidentally ruining him. Sadly that still counts as a positive relationship by First Age standards since she provably actually cares about her lunar mate despite being a lunatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:35:21-07:00","id":1295953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295950#post1295950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm wondering why it's presented in the style of a PC option, and not a QC Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to wager, its there so that STs can slap it onto Shahan-yas and other power Lunars. Its also a cool thing for players to aim for I'd guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295950#post1295950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, reading that one it says that he got turned into a mindless tentacle monster by a lab accident and the grief turned her into a crazy transhumanist who turned herself into a tentacle monster and says being a cephalopod abomination is a good thing to make herself feel better about accidentally ruining him. Sadly that still counts as a positive relationship by First Age standards since she provably actually cares about her lunar mate despite being a lunatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that isn't damning for 2ed's take I don't know what is, I think that the new direction is better for both splats as players and NPCs. Vance said something I liked in that it is hard to speak in absolute truths about the First Age and the Exalts (he said Solars but I think its fair to apply it to everyone), that is a very good thing. Your players are now very free to go in any direction they want with the bond and have it supported by canon.<br /> <br /> One of my players wants a positive tie with his solar mate in a game I'm setting up right now and I can happily say that it makes sense in 3ed, where it would have been super weird last edition. I think that Lilith is a very helpful guideline to new players and STs with how to positively frame the Bond with a Solar NPC, but that us just my take.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:00:32-07:00","id":1295961,"title":"","content":"It could always be worse, they could have been a 2nd edition Dragonblooded and had to deal with things like 'all gods will instinctively always consider them as being lower then mortals and never respect them because at least a mortal has a chance of becoming a <i>real</i> exalt and its impossible to ever convince them otherwise because its a metaphysical fact woven into the very fabric of reality by the Creation Ruling Mandate and therefore so super true you might as well try to convince them left is right'* along with other such shade thrown their way.<br /> <br /> *Compass Yu-Shan page 34 big honking sidebar dedicated entirely to that subject","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:08:21-07:00","id":1295962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295961#post1295961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could always be worse, they could have been a 2nd edition Dragonblooded and had to deal with things like 'all gods will instinctively always consider them as being lower then mortals and never respect them because at least a mortal has a chance of becoming a <i>real</i> exalt and its impossible to ever convince them otherwise because its a metaphysical fact woven into the very fabric of reality by the Creation Ruling Mandate and therefore so super true you might as well try to convince them left is right'* along with other such shade thrown their way.<br /> <br /> *Compass Yu-Shan page 34 big honking sidebar dedicated entirely to that subject</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was more that many of the gods saw them as traitors and usurpers, like Yu-Shan did with Bronze Faction Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:11:25-07:00","id":1295963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295950#post1295950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm wondering why it's presented in the style of a PC option, and not a QC Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly because there's not a fully written out version in the Charms chapter that can be referenced if the QC version is ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:15:16-07:00","id":1295965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295961#post1295961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could always be worse, they could have been a 2nd edition Dragonblooded and had to deal with things like 'all gods will instinctively always consider them as being lower then mortals and never respect them because at least a mortal has a chance of becoming a <i>real</i> exalt and its impossible to ever convince them otherwise because its a metaphysical fact woven into the very fabric of reality by the Creation Ruling Mandate and therefore so super true you might as well try to convince them left is right'* along with other such shade thrown their way.<br /> <br /> *Compass Yu-Shan page 34 big honking sidebar dedicated entirely to that subject</div> </div> </div> </div>That was from 1e, word for word like most of what was riped from sidereals and just sloppily bolted on to if I remember correctly. It's been a while but almost all of what wasn't attempting to undercut sidereals was just a direct copy and paste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:22:02-07:00","id":1295970,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295962#post1295962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was more that many of the gods saw them as traitors and usurpers, like Yu-Shan did with Bronze Faction Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, thats just what those sidereal dummies who don't know anything think when they wonder why literally every single god ever without a single exception disdains them! Its a metaphysical fact of reality that they are big stupid losers who, regardless of accomplishment, are less worthy of respect then even the poorest and most ill educated of street urchins because at least the urchin has an infinitesimal chance of becoming a <i>real</i> exalt! And the sad thing is I'm not exaggerating in the slightest. Not going to post the entire sidebar since thats probably too much for fair use but here is the part explaining how its metaphysical fact and no amount of personal success will ever convince a single solitary god any dragon blooded is worth anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The truth of the matter lies in the Creation-<br /> Ruling Mandate handed down by the<br /> Unconquered Sun to his Exalted children, establishing<br /> the inherent right of the Solar Exalted to<br /> rule in his name. Although the Mandate was the<br /> Unconquered Sun\u2019s to hand down, the Mandate<br /> also had the support of the other Incarnae, and<br /> as a result, the right to rule became inherent in<br /> the Celestial Exalted, and this right was woven<br /> into the very fabric of Creation. Consequently,<br /> it was woven into the very fabric of the gods,<br /> as well.<br /> As a result, all gods, even those who supported<br /> the Usurpation whether for altruistic<br /> or selfish reasons, instinctively know that the<br /> Usurpation defied the natural order, which<br /> demands that the Celestial Exalted rule Creation.<br /> Dragon-Blooded may have ruled Creation<br /> during the Shogunate, and they may yet rule<br /> all Creation again. But for all their power and<br /> wealth and influence, no Dragon-Blood will<br /> ever hold the respect that a god will instinctively<br /> have for the lowliest street urchin. It<br /> is possible, however unlikely, that the dirty<br /> street urchin might someday receive Celestial<br /> Exaltation. By their very natures, no Dragon-<br /> Blood ever will </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In 2nd edition anyway, thank god that shit has been thrown in a fire in 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I guess it was apparently true in 1E as well? Wasn't around for it and never got around to reading a lot of its material with a few exceptions like Scavengers Sons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-11-2019, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:27:20-07:00","id":1295973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295970#post1295970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: And I guess it was apparently true in 1E as well? Wasn't around for it and never got around to reading a lot of its material with a few exceptions like Scavengers Sons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can check it again. I do remember that passage though it was pretty much the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:29:48-07:00","id":1295974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295970#post1295970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope, thats just what those sidereal dummies who don't know anything think when they wonder why literally every single god ever without a single exception disdains them! Its a metaphysical fact of reality that they are big stupid losers who, regardless of accomplishment, are less worthy of respect then even the poorest and most ill educated of street urchins because at least the urchin has an infinitesimal chance of becoming a <i>real</i> exalt! And the sad thing is I'm not exaggerating in the slightest. Not going to post the entire sidebar since thats probably too much for fair use but here is the part explaining how its metaphysical fact and no amount of personal success will ever convince a god any dragon blooded is worth anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In 2nd edition anyway, thank god that shit has been thrown in a fire in 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I guess it was apparently true in 1E as well? Wasn't around for it and never got around to reading a lot of its material with a few exceptions like Scavengers Sons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont want to sink into a splat-debate but I always point out that gods tend to be dicks that most DB PCs can pretty quickly slaughter. That and the DBs largely being the ones to curb their excesses. So it was always more of a triumphant underdog angle, I am profoundly disturbed when folks act as if its preferable to be a powerful rapist than a triumphant underdog narratively.<br /> <br /> But fortunately, that is all in the dark past and we can focus now on the bright future.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, how has no one mentioned thr best thing about Lilith? Her default description includes a helmet! I know Exalted will be exalted but I cant recall the last time we had a powerful figure actually bother to account for proper head-protection.<br /> <br /> Well, that and I am an unrepentent fan of cool helmets. It actually combines well with her being an old warrior with Owl tones for an Athena vibe.<br /> <br /> Edit:Hmm, might slap a Moonsilver Thunderbolt Shield and Longfang on her to complete the look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-11-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:34:28-07:00","id":1295975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295973#post1295973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can check it again. I do remember that passage though it was pretty much the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine taking your word for it, though its always interesting to see how the basic concept of exalted is just so awesome it kept going despite sometimes having the specifics get messed up when given focus by past editions.<br /> <br /> Its true, I was so focused on the rewrite of her past I didn't notice she wears a helmet. Truly she is a trend setter even after taking such a long vacation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T16:41:45-07:00","id":1295976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295975#post1295975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine taking your word for it, though its always interesting to see how the basic concept of exalted is just so awesome it kept going despite sometimes having the specifics get messed up when given focus by past editions.<br /> <br /> Its true, I was so focused on the rewrite of her past I didn't notice she wears a helmet. Truly she is a trend setter even after taking such a long vacation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more you think about it, the more Lunar Athena sort of works for her. I also dont think the Athena archetype (Calm, blunt War-Goddess with a thing for helmets and owls) has been used in exalted yet.<br /> <br /> Also I weirdly want a hoplite Shahan-ya so it works for me lol.<br /> <br /> By the by, we are almost in for the last 48 tidal wave. We might well see the Lunars end higher than DBs yet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-11-2019, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:56:01-07:00","id":1295994,"title":"","content":"260K reached, we are getting a write up of necromancy leopard and their domain thats going to be really useful when I eventually play a lunar necromancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T18:03:13-07:00","id":1295997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295994#post1295994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">260K reached, we are getting a write up of necromancy leopard and their domain thats going to be really useful when I eventually play a lunar necromancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that we have two big Lunar necromancers with different pact dynamics, gives more options to a necromancer Lunar PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T23:57:48-07:00","id":1296059,"title":"","content":"Ok everyone. We're 9K away. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=180YLV4b5Nw\" target=\"_blank\">Let's get dangerous.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T01:10:36-07:00","id":1296068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295921#post1295921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't believe we have 2 pages of Lilith discussion and no one's mentioned seeing our first example of an Essence 6 Elder Exalted charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can believe it. <br /> <br /> Anyway, building excitement, gif of that guy who foams at the mouth in Avatar, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T05:16:26-07:00","id":1296097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295662#post1295662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked about a possibility for this on the new Ask Devs thread, and Vance agreed that making inherent human traits into mutations that can be applied to animal forms with Perfect Hybrid Interaction is a viable option. So just make human speech a 1 or 2 dot mutation. Much more cost effective than dedicating a Charm for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This approach requires dedicating mutation points from the limited pool Perfected Hybrid Interaction gives you, which is only 4 per Essence dot. I'd rather it was a separate Charm. <br /> <br /> I also like the new Lilith and the &quot;not perfect but ultimately solid marriage&quot; angle. We needed one of those. I find it odd that they would re-invent Lilith's Solar from the ground up rather than try to rehabilitate Desus. Though I can't really say I'm sad to see him go either.<br /> <br /> I guess he isn't as integral to the setting as some of the previous editions' monstrous psychos, like Raksi, who got a more nuanced or sympathetic portrayal this go-around. And of course, eating babies is so obviously monstrous and vile that everyone can agree it's a bad thing, whereas domestic abuse is something far, far too many assholes do, and don't need a model for in exalted canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T06:22:04-07:00","id":1296106,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2442878\" target=\"_blank\">So, final chapter up</a>, with new Essence 6 Charms for the elders (Lilith, which we've already seen, Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi).<br /> <br /> And I note re: Lilith discussion that her tie to Andamani is Ambivalence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T06:43:13-07:00","id":1296108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1296097#post1296097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like the new Lilith and the &quot;not perfect but ultimately solid marriage&quot; angle. We needed one of those. I find it odd that they would re-invent Lilith's Solar from the ground up rather than try to rehabilitate Desus. Though I can't really say I'm sad to see him go either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain Desus wasn't her mate until late in First Edition. Her mate's identity was undefined through her first appearances. In the corebook for Exalted First Edition, it notes that they had a relationship with some serious ups and downs. I think this description could still adequately describe her relationship with Andamani. In Exalted: the Lunars, the fiction added a lot of cruel details and talked about how she'd probably kill her still unnamed Solar Mate if she could. I don't think this second fiction describes her relationship with Andamani particularly well.<br /> <br /> Desus was invented for an Odyssey reference in <i>Creatures of the Wyld</i> and then appeared in a few more places. He didn't appear in Swan's backstory given in Castebook Eclipse, but then in the novels, he became Swan's previous incarnation and thus Lilith's mate.<br /> <br /> And then in Second Edition it got worse.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Altered my post to reflect information I've learned since writing this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":23657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","user":"VioletDreamer","date":". 03-13-2019, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T06:48:28-07:00","id":1296110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295970#post1295970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And I guess it was apparently true in 1E as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find it.<br /> Exalted: The Sidereals wasn't exactly respectful to Dragon-Blooded and points out that as far as Yu-Shan is concerned they're walking property so it's not a difference in tone. <br /> <br /> As far as I can tell-<br /> -Second Edition started talking about the Mandate of Heaven as a distinct <i>thing</i> which here informs the opinions of the gods like they're robots.<br /> -Compass Yu-Shan is considered worse because part of the goal of making it a seperate book was to make it less of an impenetrable Sidereal club house so the stuff about Dragon-Blooded seemed notably mean spirited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T10:04:31-07:00","id":1296168,"title":"","content":"Raksi's Essence 6 Elder Charm <b>Witch-Queen\u2019s Midnight Crown</b> is amazeballs. It kind of feels in a class of it's own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T12:56:53-07:00","id":1296209,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1296110#post1296110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find it.<br /> Exalted: The Sidereals wasn't exactly respectful to Dragon-Blooded and points out that as far as Yu-Shan is concerned they're walking property so it's not a difference in tone.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell-<br /> -Second Edition started talking about the Mandate of Heaven as a distinct <i>thing</i> which here informs the opinions of the gods like they're robots.<br /> -Compass Yu-Shan is considered worse because part of the goal of making it a seperate book was to make it less of an impenetrable Sidereal club house so the stuff about Dragon-Blooded seemed notably mean spirited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez, they wrote that in a book that was from a development stand point supposed to be about making Heaven <i>more accessible</i> to exalts that weren't Sidereals? That really does seem incredibly mean spirited. Did a dragon blooded jump out of the book and set the writers dog on fire or something?<br /> <br /> Poor second edition spirit robots, no free will of their own. Forced to not only hate amazing elemental heroes who could probably kick their ass for disrespecting them and also forced to respect every human ever. Must have made it incredibly hard to be a corrupt self serving dick when your operating system forced you to respect the people you were trying to extort for more prayers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1296168#post1296168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi's Essence 6 Elder Charm <b>Witch-Queen\u2019s Midnight Crown</b> is amazeballs. It kind of feels in a class of it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it was definitely amazing. And apparently in this edition she has achieved her dream of being able to use solar circle sorcery via Book of 3 Circles evocations so maybe thats why she is slightly less of a bitch.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Huh, interesting, so this edition Lilith is a casteless who never received a tattoo locking her caste in. So thats one 1st age elder for each caste choice, I think.<br /> <br /> edit edit: Wait, Leviathan is a full moon, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-12-2019, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T16:06:22-07:00","id":1296260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1295974#post1295974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont want to sink into a splat-debate but I always point out that gods tend to be dicks that most DB PCs can pretty quickly slaughter. That and the DBs largely being the ones to curb their excesses. So it was always more of a triumphant underdog angle</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e version as I recall was more well worded, to clearly be kindred of the general (and snobbish) bias of the Celestial gods against elementals and their bias in favour of the Incarna. <br /> <br /> It felt like it fit with the Dragonblooded's framing as the frequently underestimated &quot;lowest&quot; among the Exalted, and frowned on by a fairly unjustly snooty Celestial order that under-recognizes their accomplishments (for all that these are lesser in scope than the Celestials, they are more to aid Creation than most among the decadent Celestial Bureaucracy can honestly say they provide). Cue much unexpected Terrestrial wins against Celestial gods and that anime &quot;How.... how... can this be?!&quot; thing. It's there for you to feel satisfaction as a DB player when some god dismisses you as a &quot;mere Terrestrial&quot; and you show them that you're not. (&quot;Triumphant underdog&quot;).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I feel like the 2e wording may have lost some of that vibe.<br /> <br /> (Like, this is the framing I got out of it... but in fairness very few people have ever defended it this way on an Exalted forum as far as I can remember, so no perhaps this is not a consensual framing!).<br /> <br /> There are limits to that sort of thing when you have many gods openly backing the Realm as legitimate though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T11:46:56-07:00","id":1296468,"title":"","content":"Ok, by my count, we\u2019ve gotten seven pieces of chapter fiction and the book has nine chapters. Did I miss a couple or have they not posted all of them yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T13:20:45-07:00","id":1296490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1296209#post1296209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez, they wrote that in a book that was from a development stand point supposed to be about making Heaven <i>more accessible</i> to exalts that weren't Sidereals? That really does seem incredibly mean spirited. Did a dragon blooded jump out of the book and set the writers dog on fire or something?<br /> <br /> Poor second edition spirit robots, no free will of their own. Forced to not only hate amazing elemental heroes who could probably kick their ass for disrespecting them and also forced to respect every human ever. Must have made it incredibly hard to be a corrupt self serving dick when your operating system forced you to respect the people you were trying to extort for more prayers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was interpreted as &quot;make Yu-Shan more Solar friendly&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T14:03:44-07:00","id":1296506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1283424-lunars-kickstarter-february-12th?p=1296490#post1296490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"m